<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<usx version="3.1">
<book code="PRO" style="id">BLB-Draft</book>

<para style="h">Proverbs</para>

<para style="toc1">Proverbs</para>

<para style="rem">sourceUrl=https://literalbible.com/blb.docx fetchedAtUtc=2026-09-01T15:43:00Z status=draft id=BLB-Draft spec=USFM-USX 3.1.1 char:add=docx-italic note:f=docx-footnotes note:x=docx-heading-crossrefs</para>

<chapter number="1" style="c" sid="PRO 1"/>

<para style="s">The Beginning of Knowledge</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 1:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Proverbs 9:1–12</char></note>The proverbs of Solomon son of David, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 1:1">king of Israel: <verse eid="PRO 1:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 1:2"/>For knowing wisdom and discipline, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 1:2">for discerning words of understanding, <verse eid="PRO 1:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 1:3"/>for receiving the instruction of wisdom, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 1:3">righteousness, and justice, and uprightness, <verse eid="PRO 1:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 1:4"/>for giving to the simple ones<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> The Hebrew word rendered </char><char style="fq" closed="false">simple</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> in Proverbs refers to one who is naive, without moral direction, or inclined to evil.</char></note> prudence, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 1:4">to a youth knowledge and discretion. <verse eid="PRO 1:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 1:5"/>Let the wise hear and add to instruction, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 1:5">and the discerning acquire wise counsel, <verse eid="PRO 1:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 1:6"/>to understand a proverb and a parable, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 1:6">the words of the wise ones and their riddles. <verse eid="PRO 1:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 1:7"/>The fear of YHWH <char style="add">is</char> the beginning of knowledge; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 1:7">wisdom and instruction fools<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> The Hebrew words rendered as </char><char style="fq" closed="false">fool</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> in Proverbs denote one who is morally deficient.</char></note> have despised. <verse eid="PRO 1:7"/></para>

<para style="s">The Enticement of Sin</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 1:8"/>Hear, my son, the discipline of your father, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 1:8">and do not forsake the instruction of your mother. <verse eid="PRO 1:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 1:9"/>For a garland of grace they <char style="add">are</char> to your head, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 1:9">and pendants for your neck. <verse eid="PRO 1:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 1:10"/>My son, if sinners should entice you, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 1:10">do not be willing. <verse eid="PRO 1:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 1:11"/>If they say, “Come with us, let us lie in wait for blood, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 1:11">let us hide for the innocent one without cause; <verse eid="PRO 1:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 1:12"/>let us swallow them alive like Sheol, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 1:12">and whole like those descending into the Pit; <verse eid="PRO 1:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 1:13"/>all precious wealth we will find, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 1:13">we will fill our houses with plunder; <verse eid="PRO 1:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 1:14"/>let your lot fall in our midst—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 1:14">one purse there shall be for all of us!”— <verse eid="PRO 1:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 1:15"/>My son, do not walk in the way with them; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 1:15">withhold your foot from their path; <verse eid="PRO 1:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 1:16"/>for their feet run to evil, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 1:16">and they are swift to shed blood. <verse eid="PRO 1:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 1:17"/>For the net is spread in vain </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 1:17">in the eyes of any owner of the wing, <verse eid="PRO 1:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 1:18"/>and they lie in wait for their own blood; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 1:18">they lurk for their own souls. <verse eid="PRO 1:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 1:19"/>Such <char style="add">are</char> the ways of everyone being greedy for dishonest gain—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 1:19">the soul of its masters it takes away. <verse eid="PRO 1:19"/></para>

<para style="s">Wisdom Calls Aloud</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 1:20"/>Wisdom calls aloud in the street; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 1:20">in the open squares she gives forth her voice. <verse eid="PRO 1:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 1:21"/>At the head of the clamoring<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.21 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">From the top of the wall</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">In the main concourse</char></note> she cries out; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 1:21">at the openings of the gates in the city she speaks her words: <verse eid="PRO 1:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 1:22"/>“Until when, O simple ones, will you⁺ love simplicity, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 1:22">and those mocking delight themselves in mockery, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 1:22">and the foolish ones hate knowledge? <verse eid="PRO 1:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 1:23"/>Turn back at my rebuke; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 1:23">behold, I will pour out on you⁺ my spirit; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 1:23">I will make known my words to you⁺. <verse eid="PRO 1:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 1:24"/>Because I have called and you⁺ refused, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 1:24">I have stretched out my hand, and no one is paying attention; <verse eid="PRO 1:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 1:25"/>and you⁺ have neglected all my counsel, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 1:25">and you⁺ did not consent to my rebuke. <verse eid="PRO 1:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 1:26"/>I also will laugh at your⁺ calamity; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 1:26">I will mock the coming of your⁺ dread; <verse eid="PRO 1:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 1:27"/>your⁺ dread comes like a storm, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 1:27">and your⁺ calamity like a whirlwind comes, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 1:27">in the coming upon you⁺ of distress and anguish. <verse eid="PRO 1:27"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 1:28"/>Then they will call on me, and I will not answer; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 1:28">they will seek me diligently, and they will not find me, <verse eid="PRO 1:28"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PRO 1:29"/>upon that they hated knowledge </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 1:29">and they have not choosen the fear of YHWH. <verse eid="PRO 1:29"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PRO 1:30"/>They did not consent to my counsel; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 1:30">they have despised all my reproof. <verse eid="PRO 1:30"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PRO 1:31"/>And they shall eat the fruit of their own way, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 1:31">and from their own counsels they shall be filled. <verse eid="PRO 1:31"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PRO 1:32"/>For the turning away of the simple ones slays them, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 1:32">and the complacency of fools destroys them. <verse eid="PRO 1:32"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="PRO 1:33"/>And the one listening to me will dwell <char style="add">in</char> safety, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 1:33">and will be at ease from the dread of evil.” <verse eid="PRO 1:33"/></para>

<chapter eid="PRO 1"/>

<chapter number="2" style="c" sid="PRO 2"/>

<para style="s">The Benefits of Wisdom</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 2:1"/>My son, if you receive my words </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 2:1">and you treasure my commands within you, <verse eid="PRO 2:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 2:2"/>to make your ear attentive to wisdom, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 2:2">you incline your heart to understanding. <verse eid="PRO 2:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 2:3"/>For if you call out for understanding, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 2:3"><char style="add">and</char> for insight you give forth your voice, <verse eid="PRO 2:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 2:4"/>if you seek her like silver, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 2:4">and like hidden treasures you search for her, <verse eid="PRO 2:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 2:5"/>then you will understand the fear of YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 2:5">and the knowledge of God you will find. <verse eid="PRO 2:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 2:6"/>For YHWH gives wisdom; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 2:6">from His mouth <char style="add">is</char> knowledge and understanding. <verse eid="PRO 2:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 2:7"/>He stores up for the upright good sense—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 2:7">protection for those walking with integrity. <verse eid="PRO 2:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 2:8"/>He watches over the paths of justice, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 2:8">and the way of His holy ones He guards. <verse eid="PRO 2:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 2:9"/>Then you will understand righteousness and justice and uprightness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 2:9">every good path. <verse eid="PRO 2:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 2:10"/>For wisdom will enter into your heart, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 2:10">and knowledge will be pleasant to your soul. <verse eid="PRO 2:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 2:11"/>Discretion will guard over you; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 2:11">understanding will guard you, <verse eid="PRO 2:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 2:12"/>to snatch you from the way of evil, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 2:12">from the man speaking perversity— <verse eid="PRO 2:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 2:13"/>those abandoning the paths of uprightness </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 2:13">to walk in the ways of darkness, <verse eid="PRO 2:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 2:14"/>those glad to do evil, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 2:14">they rejoice in the perversity of evil, <verse eid="PRO 2:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 2:15"/>whose ways <char style="add">are</char> crooked, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 2:15">and <char style="add">who</char> are turning aside in their paths. <verse eid="PRO 2:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 2:16"/>It will deliver you from a strange woman,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.16 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">from a wayward wife</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 2:16">from a foreign woman<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.16 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">from an adulteress</char></note> having made smooth her words, <verse eid="PRO 2:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 2:17"/>the one having forsaken the guide of her youth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 2:17">and she has forgotten the covenant of her God. <verse eid="PRO 2:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 2:18"/>For her house sinks down to death, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 2:18">and her paths to the Rephaim.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.18 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, </char><char style="fq" closed="false">to the departed spirits</char></note> <verse eid="PRO 2:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 2:19"/>Of all those coming to her, none will return, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 2:19">nor will they reach the paths of life. <verse eid="PRO 2:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 2:20"/>So you must walk in the way of the good ones, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 2:20">and guard the paths of the righteous ones. <verse eid="PRO 2:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 2:21"/>For the upright will dwell in the land, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 2:21">and the blameless ones will remain in it. <verse eid="PRO 2:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 2:22"/>And the wicked will be cut off from the earth, and treacherous ones </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 2:22">will be plucked out from it. <verse eid="PRO 2:22"/></para>

<chapter eid="PRO 2"/>

<chapter number="3" style="c" sid="PRO 3"/>

<para style="s">Trust in Yahweh with All Your Heart</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 3:1"/>My son, do not forget my instruction, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 3:1">and let your heart keep my commands. <verse eid="PRO 3:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 3:2"/>For length of days and years of life and peace </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 3:2">they will add to you. <verse eid="PRO 3:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 3:3"/>And do not let loving devotion<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Forms of the Hebrew </char><char style="fq" closed="false">chesed</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> are translated here and in most cases throughout the Scriptures as </char><char style="fq" closed="false">loving devotion</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; the range of meaning includes </char><char style="fq" closed="false">love</char><char style="ft" closed="false">, </char><char style="fq" closed="false">goodness</char><char style="ft" closed="false">, </char><char style="fq" closed="false">kindness</char><char style="ft" closed="false">, </char><char style="fq" closed="false">faithfulness</char><char style="ft" closed="false">, and </char><char style="fq" closed="false">mercy</char><char style="ft" closed="false">, as well as </char><char style="fq" closed="false">loyalty to a covenant</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> and faithfulness forsake you; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 3:3">bind them around your neck; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 3:3">write them on the tablet of your heart. <verse eid="PRO 3:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 3:4"/>And you will find favor and good understanding </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 3:4">in the eyes of God and man. <verse eid="PRO 3:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 3:5"/>Put your trust unto YHWH with all your heart, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 3:5">and lean not unto your own understanding. <verse eid="PRO 3:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 3:6"/>In all your ways acknowledge Him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 3:6">and He will make straight your paths. <verse eid="PRO 3:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 3:7"/>Do not be wise in your own eyes, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 3:7">fear YHWH and turn away from evil. <verse eid="PRO 3:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 3:8"/>Healing it will be to your navel, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 3:8">and refreshment to your bones. <verse eid="PRO 3:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 3:9"/>Honor YHWH from your wealth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 3:9">and from the first of all your produce, <verse eid="PRO 3:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 3:10"/>and your barns will be filled with plenty, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 3:10">and your vats will overflow with new wine. <verse eid="PRO 3:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 3:11"/>My son, do not despise the discipline of YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 3:11">and do not be grieved by His reproof, <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3.11 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> LXX </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and do not lose heart when He rebukes</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; cited in Hebrews 12:5</char></note><verse eid="PRO 3:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 3:12"/>for whom YHWH loves, He reproves, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 3:12">even as a father the son he is pleased with.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3.12 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> LXX </char><char style="fq" closed="false">For whom the Lord loves, he rebukes, and He flogs every son He receives</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; cited in Hebrews 12:6</char></note> <verse eid="PRO 3:12"/></para>

<para style="s">The Blessings of Wisdom</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 3:13"/>Blessed <char style="add">is</char> the man <char style="add">who</char> has found wisdom, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 3:13">and the man <char style="add">who</char> brings forth understanding, <verse eid="PRO 3:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 3:14"/>for better <char style="add">is</char> the profit from her than profits of silver, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 3:14">and her produce than fine gold. <verse eid="PRO 3:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 3:15"/>Precious she <char style="add">is</char> above rubies, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 3:15">and all your delights do not compare with her. <verse eid="PRO 3:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 3:16"/>Length of days <char style="add">is</char> in her right hand, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 3:16"><char style="add">and</char> in her left hand <char style="add">are</char> wealth and honor. <verse eid="PRO 3:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 3:17"/>Her ways <char style="add">are</char> ways of pleasantness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 3:17">and all her paths <char style="add">are</char> peace. <verse eid="PRO 3:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 3:18"/>A tree of life she <char style="add">is</char> to those taking hold on her, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 3:18">and those grasping her are blessed. <verse eid="PRO 3:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 3:19"/>YHWH by wisdom founded the earth; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 3:19">He established the heavens by understanding; <verse eid="PRO 3:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 3:20"/>by His knowledge the depths have been broken up, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 3:20">and the clouds dripped dew. <verse eid="PRO 3:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 3:21"/>My son, do not do let them depart from your eyes; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 3:21">keep watch over wisdom and discretion, <verse eid="PRO 3:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 3:22"/>and they will be life for your soul, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 3:22">and grace for your neck. <verse eid="PRO 3:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 3:23"/>Then you will walk your way in safety, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 3:23">and your foot will not stumble. <verse eid="PRO 3:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 3:24"/>If you lie down, you will not dread; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 3:24">and you have lain down, and your sleep shall be pleasant. <verse eid="PRO 3:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 3:25"/>Do not be afraid from sudden dread, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 3:25">and from the desolation of the wicked when it comes. <verse eid="PRO 3:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 3:26"/>For YHWH is at your flank, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 3:26">and He will guard your foot from capture. <verse eid="PRO 3:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 3:27"/>Do not withhold good from its owners,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3.27 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">from the deserving</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 3:27">with it being in the power of your hand to act. <verse eid="PRO 3:27"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 3:28"/>You must not say to your neighbor, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 3:28">“Go and return, and tomorrow I will give”—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 3:28">and it is with you. <verse eid="PRO 3:28"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PRO 3:29"/>Do not devise evil against your neighbor, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 3:29">for he is dwelling in trust with you. <verse eid="PRO 3:29"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PRO 3:30"/>Do not strive with a man without cause, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 3:30">if he has not dealt with you <char style="add">for</char> evil. <verse eid="PRO 3:30"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PRO 3:31"/>Do not be envious of a man of violence, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 3:31">and do not choose any of his ways. <verse eid="PRO 3:31"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PRO 3:32"/>For a perverse one <char style="add">is</char> an abomination <char style="add">to</char> YHWH, and with </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 3:32">the upright <char style="add">is</char> His secret counsel. <verse eid="PRO 3:32"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="PRO 3:33"/>The curse of YHWH <char style="add">is</char> on the house of the wicked one, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 3:33">but the abode of the righteous He blesses. <verse eid="PRO 3:33"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="PRO 3:34"/>If He mocks at those mocking, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 3:34">then He gives favor to the humble. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3.34 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> LXX </char><char style="fq" closed="false">The Lord opposes the proud, but gives grace to the humble</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; cited in James 4:6 and 1 Peter 5:5</char></note><verse eid="PRO 3:34"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="PRO 3:35"/>The wise will inherit honor, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 3:35">and fools are held up <char style="add">to</char> disgrace. <verse eid="PRO 3:35"/></para>

<chapter eid="PRO 3"/>

<chapter number="4" style="c" sid="PRO 4"/>

<para style="s">A Father’s Instruction</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 4:1"/>Hear, <char style="add">my</char> sons, the discipline of a father, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 4:1">and pay attention to know understanding. <verse eid="PRO 4:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 4:2"/>For good teaching I have given to you⁺; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 4:2">do not forsake my instruction. <verse eid="PRO 4:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 4:3"/>For I was a son to my father, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 4:3">tender and the only one before the face of my mother, <verse eid="PRO 4:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 4:4"/>and he instructed me and said to me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 4:4">“Let your heart take hold of my words; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 4:4">keep my commands, and live. <verse eid="PRO 4:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 4:5"/>Acquire wisdom; acquire understanding! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 4:5">Do not forget and do not bend away from the words of my mouth. <verse eid="PRO 4:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 4:6"/>Do not forsake her, and she will preserve you; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 4:6">love her, and she will guard you. <verse eid="PRO 4:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 4:7"/>The first <char style="add">thing</char> <char style="add">is</char> wisdom; acquire wisdom, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 4:7">and in all your acquiring,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">And whatever else you acquire</char></note> acquire understanding. <verse eid="PRO 4:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 4:8"/>Lift her up, and she will exalt you; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 4:8">she will bring you honor when you embrace her. <verse eid="PRO 4:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 4:9"/>She will give to your head a wreath of grace; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 4:9">a crown of beauty she will deliver to you.” <verse eid="PRO 4:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 4:10"/>Hear, my son, and receive my sayings, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 4:10">and the years of life will be multiplied for you. <verse eid="PRO 4:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 4:11"/>In the way of wisdom I have instructed you; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 4:11">I have made you step in paths of uprightness. <verse eid="PRO 4:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 4:12"/>In your walking, your steps will not be restricted; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 4:12">and when you run, you will not stumble. <verse eid="PRO 4:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 4:13"/>Hold on to instruction; do not let go; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 4:13">Guard her, for she <char style="add">is</char> your life. <verse eid="PRO 4:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 4:14"/>Do not enter into the path of the wicked ones, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 4:14">and do not walk in the way of evil ones. <verse eid="PRO 4:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 4:15"/>Avoid it! Do not pass onto it; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 4:15">turn aside from it and pass by. <verse eid="PRO 4:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 4:16"/>For they cannot sleep </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 4:16">if they have not done evil; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PRO 4:16">and their sleep is stolen </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 4:16">if they do not they cause stumbling. <verse eid="PRO 4:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 4:17"/>Indeed, they eat the bread of wickedness; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 4:17">they drink the wine of violence. <verse eid="PRO 4:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 4:18"/>But the path of the righteous is like the light of brightness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 4:18">and shining and going forth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 4:18">until the day is established. <verse eid="PRO 4:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 4:19"/>The way of the wicked <char style="add">is</char> like the darkness—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 4:19">they do not know over what they stumble. <verse eid="PRO 4:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 4:20"/>My son, pay attention to my words; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 4:20">incline your ear to my sayings. <verse eid="PRO 4:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 4:21"/>Do not let them depart from your eyes—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 4:21">keep them in the midst of your heart. <verse eid="PRO 4:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 4:22"/>For they <char style="add">are</char> life to those finding them, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 4:22">and to all his flesh healing. <verse eid="PRO 4:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 4:23"/>With all diligence, guard your heart, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 4:23">for from it <char style="add">are</char> the outgoings of life. <verse eid="PRO 4:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 4:24"/>Turn away from you the crookedness of the mouth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 4:24">and perverse lips put far from you. <verse eid="PRO 4:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 4:25"/>Your eyes should look forward, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 4:25">and your eyelids keep straight before you. <verse eid="PRO 4:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 4:26"/>Make level the path for your feet, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 4:26">and all your ways shall be established. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.26 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Ponder the path for your feet</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; LXX </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Make straight paths for your feet</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; cited in Hebrews 12:13</char></note><verse eid="PRO 4:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 4:27"/>Do not bend away to the right or the left; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 4:27">turn aside your foot from evil. <verse eid="PRO 4:27"/></para>

<chapter eid="PRO 4"/>

<chapter number="5" style="c" sid="PRO 5"/>

<para style="s">Avoiding Immorality</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 5:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">1 Corinthians 5:1–8</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Leviticus 20:10–21</char></note>My son, pay attention to my wisdom, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 5:1"><char style="add">and</char> to my understanding incline your ear, <verse eid="PRO 5:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 5:2"/>to keep discretion, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 5:2">and <char style="add">that</char> your lips may guard knowledge. <verse eid="PRO 5:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 5:3"/>For the lips of the forbidden woman<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">5.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">of the adulteress</char></note> drip honey, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 5:3">and smoother than oil <char style="add">is</char> her palate;<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">5.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">her speech</char></note> <verse eid="PRO 5:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 5:4"/>but her end <char style="add">is</char> bitter as wormwood, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 5:4">sharp <char style="add">with</char> mouths as a sword. <verse eid="PRO 5:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 5:5"/>Her feet go down to death; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 5:5">her steps lay hold of sheol.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">5.5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">lead straight to Sheol</char></note> <verse eid="PRO 5:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 5:6"/>The path of life she does not weigh; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 5:6">her tracks are unstable; she does not know <char style="add">it</char>. <verse eid="PRO 5:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 5:7"/>And now, sons, listen to me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 5:7">and do not turn aside from the words of my mouth. <verse eid="PRO 5:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 5:8"/>Keep your path far away from her, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 5:8">and do not go near to the opening of her house, <verse eid="PRO 5:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 5:9"/>lest you give to others your splendor, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 5:9">and your years to a cruel one; <verse eid="PRO 5:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 5:10"/>lest strangers be satisfied <char style="add">by</char> your strength, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 5:10">and your labors <char style="add">be</char> in the house of a foreigner; <verse eid="PRO 5:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 5:11"/>and you groan at your end, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 5:11">in the consumption of your flesh and your body, <verse eid="PRO 5:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 5:12"/>and you say, “How I hated discipline, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 5:12">and my heart spurned rebuke! <verse eid="PRO 5:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 5:13"/>And I have not listened to the voice of my instructors, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 5:13">and I have not inclined my ear to those teaching me. <verse eid="PRO 5:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 5:14"/>Am I as a little from all evil, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 5:14">in the midst of the assembly and the gathering.” <verse eid="PRO 5:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 5:15"/>Drink water from your own cistern </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 5:15">and flowing from the midst of your own well. <verse eid="PRO 5:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 5:16"/>Should your fountains be dispersed outside, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 5:16">channels of water in broad places? <verse eid="PRO 5:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 5:17"/>Let them be for you, yourself alone, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 5:17">and not for strangers with you. <verse eid="PRO 5:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 5:18"/>Let your fountain be blessed, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 5:18">and rejoice with the wife of your youth. <verse eid="PRO 5:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 5:19"/>A loving doe and a graceful deer, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 5:19">let her breasts satisfy you at all times—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 5:19">may you wander<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">5.19 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">be led astray</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; also in verse 20</char></note> in her love continually! <verse eid="PRO 5:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 5:20"/>So why do you wander, my son, with a strange woman, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 5:20">and embrace the bosom of a foreign woman?<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">5.20 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">of a stranger</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">of another man’s wife</char></note> <verse eid="PRO 5:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 5:21"/>For the ways of man <char style="add">are</char> in front of the eyes of YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 5:21">and all his paths He weighs.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">5.21 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">examines</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">makes level</char></note> <verse eid="PRO 5:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 5:22"/>His own iniquities capture a wicked one, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 5:22">and he is held with the cords of his sin. <verse eid="PRO 5:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 5:23"/>He shall die for lack of discipline, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 5:23">and in the abundance of his folly he shall go astray. <verse eid="PRO 5:23"/></para>

<chapter eid="PRO 5"/>

<chapter number="6" style="c" sid="PRO 6"/>

<para style="s">Warnings against Foolishness</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 6:1"/>My son, if you have been surety for your neighbor, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 6:1"><char style="add">or</char> have struck your hand for the stranger, <verse eid="PRO 6:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 6:2"/><char style="add">or</char> have been lured by the words of your mouth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 6:2">captured by the words of your mouth, <verse eid="PRO 6:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 6:3"/>then you must do this my son, and deliver yourself, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 6:3">for you have come into the palm of your neighbor: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PRO 6:3">Go humble yourself,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">6.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Go, hasten</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 6:3">and press your neighbor. <verse eid="PRO 6:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 6:4"/>You should not give sleep to your eyes </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 6:4">or slumber to your eyelids— <verse eid="PRO 6:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 6:5"/>snatch yourself like a gazelle from the hand,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">6.5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, </char><char style="fq" closed="false">from the hand of the hunter</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 6:5">and like a bird from the hand of the fowler. <verse eid="PRO 6:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 6:6"/>Go to the ant, O sluggish one; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 6:6">see her ways and become wise: <verse eid="PRO 6:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 6:7"/>Which there is not unto her a chief, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 6:7">an official, or ruler, <verse eid="PRO 6:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 6:8"/>she prepares her bread in summer, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 6:8">she has gathered her food in the harvest. <verse eid="PRO 6:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 6:9"/>Until when, O sluggish one, will you slumber? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 6:9">When will you rise from your sleep? <verse eid="PRO 6:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 6:10"/>A little sleep, a little slumber, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 6:10">a little folding of the hands to lie down, <verse eid="PRO 6:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 6:11"/>and your poverty comes like one walking, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 6:11">and your need like a man of shield. <verse eid="PRO 6:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 6:12"/>A man of worthlessness, a man of iniquity, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 6:12">is walking <char style="add">with</char> crookedness of mouth, <verse eid="PRO 6:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 6:13"/>winking with his eyes, speaking with his foot, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 6:13">pointing with his fingers, <verse eid="PRO 6:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 6:14"/><char style="add">with</char> perversity in his heart, plotting evil; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 6:14">at every time he sends forth strife. <verse eid="PRO 6:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 6:15"/>Upon thus his calamity shall come suddenly; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 6:15">in an instant he will be shattered, and without healing. <verse eid="PRO 6:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 6:16"/>These six <char style="add">things</char> YHWH hates, and seven <char style="add">are</char> an abomination to His soul: <verse eid="PRO 6:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 6:17"/>Eyes raised high, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PRO 6:17">a tongue of falsehood, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PRO 6:17">and hands pouring out innocent blood, <verse eid="PRO 6:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 6:18"/>a heart devising plans of iniquity, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PRO 6:18">feet hurrying to run toward evil, <verse eid="PRO 6:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 6:19"/>one breathing out lies, a witness of falsehood, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PRO 6:19">and one sending forth contentions between brothers. <verse eid="PRO 6:19"/></para>

<para style="s">Warnings against Adultery</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 6:20"/>Keep, my son, the command of your father, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 6:20">and do not forsake the instruction of your mother. <verse eid="PRO 6:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 6:21"/>Bind them upon your heart continually; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 6:21">tie them around your neck. <verse eid="PRO 6:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 6:22"/>In your going about, it will lead you; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 6:22">in your lying down, it will guard you; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 6:22">when you awake, it will speak with you. <verse eid="PRO 6:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 6:23"/>For the command <char style="add">is</char> a lamp, and the instruction a light, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 6:23">and the reproofs of discipline are the way to life, <verse eid="PRO 6:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 6:24"/>to guard you from the woman of evil, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 6:24">from the smoothness of the tongue of a strange woman.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">6.24 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">of an adulteress</char></note> <verse eid="PRO 6:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 6:25"/>Do not desire her beauty in your heart, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 6:25">and do not let her take hold of you with her eyelids.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">6.25 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">eyes</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">eyelashes</char></note> <verse eid="PRO 6:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 6:26"/>For the price of a woman prostitute is as a crust of bread, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 6:26">and the woman<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">6.26 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">wife</char></note> of a man hunts a precious soul. <verse eid="PRO 6:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 6:27"/>Can a man seize fire in his bosom, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 6:27">and his garments not be burned? <verse eid="PRO 6:27"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 6:28"/>Or <char style="add">can</char> a man walk upon the hot coals, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 6:28">and his feet not be scorched? <verse eid="PRO 6:28"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PRO 6:29"/>So <char style="add">is</char> the one coming in to the wife of his neighbor; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 6:29">anyone who touches her shall not be innocent. <verse eid="PRO 6:29"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PRO 6:30"/>They do not despise the thief </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 6:30">if he steals to fill his soul when he is hungry, <verse eid="PRO 6:30"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PRO 6:31"/>and having been found, he must repay sevenfold; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 6:31">all the wealth of his house he must give. <verse eid="PRO 6:31"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PRO 6:32"/>The one committing adultery with a woman is lacking of heart; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 6:32">he does it, destroying his own soul. <verse eid="PRO 6:32"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="PRO 6:33"/>He finds <char style="add">only a stroke and shame, </char></para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 6:33"><char style="add">and his reproach is not wiped away. </char><verse eid="PRO 6:33"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="PRO 6:34"/><char style="add">For jealousy is the heat of a man, </char></para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 6:34"><char style="add">and he will not spare on the day of vengeance. </char><verse eid="PRO 6:34"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="PRO 6:35"/><char style="add">He will not lift the face of any ransom, </char></para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 6:35"><char style="add">and he will not consent, though you may multiply the bribe. </char><verse eid="PRO 6:35"/></para>

<chapter eid="PRO 6"/>

<chapter number="7" style="c" sid="PRO 7"/>

<para style="s">Warnings about the Adulteress</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 7:1"/>My son, keep my words </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 7:1">and treasure my commands within you. <verse eid="PRO 7:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 7:2"/>Guard my commands and live, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 7:2">and my instruction like the pupil<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7.2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the apple</char></note> of your eyes. <verse eid="PRO 7:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 7:3"/>Bind them on your fingers; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 7:3">write them on the tablet of your heart. <verse eid="PRO 7:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 7:4"/>Say to wisdom, “You <char style="add">are</char> my sister,” </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 7:4">and call out to understanding, “Kinsman,” <verse eid="PRO 7:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 7:5"/>to guard you from the strange woman, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 7:5">from a foreign woman <char style="add">who</char> has made smooth her words. <verse eid="PRO 7:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 7:6"/>For at the window of my house </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 7:6">I have looked through my lattice, <verse eid="PRO 7:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 7:7"/>and I have looked among the simple, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 7:7"><char style="add">and</char> discerned among the sons </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 7:7">a young man lacking heart, <verse eid="PRO 7:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 7:8"/>passing by on the street near her corner, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 7:8">and the way of her house he steps in— <verse eid="PRO 7:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 7:9"/>in the twilight, in the evening <char style="add">of</char> the day, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 7:9">in the pupil of night and darkness. <verse eid="PRO 7:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 7:10"/>And behold, a woman to meet him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 7:10"><char style="add">in</char> the garment of a prostitute and guarded of heart. <verse eid="PRO 7:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 7:11"/>She <char style="add">is</char> roaring and rebellious; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 7:11">in her house her feet do not dwell. <verse eid="PRO 7:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 7:12"/>Once in the street, once in the open squares, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 7:12">and beside every corner she lies in wait. <verse eid="PRO 7:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 7:13"/>And she laid hold on him and kissed him; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 7:13">she has hardened her face and said to him: <verse eid="PRO 7:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 7:14"/>“Sacrifices of peace offerings <char style="add">are</char> by me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 7:14">this day I have paid my vows; <verse eid="PRO 7:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 7:15"/>upon thus I have come out to meet you, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 7:15">to earnestly seek your face, and I have found you! <verse eid="PRO 7:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 7:16"/>With coverings I have spread my couch, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 7:16"><char style="add">with</char> colored linen of Egypt. <verse eid="PRO 7:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 7:17"/>I have sprinkled my bed with myrrh, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 7:17">aloes, and cinnamon. <verse eid="PRO 7:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 7:18"/>Come, let us take our fill of love until the morning; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 7:18">let us delight ourselves with loves! <verse eid="PRO 7:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 7:19"/>For the husband is not in his house; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 7:19">he has gone far away on a road. <verse eid="PRO 7:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 7:20"/>A bag of silver he has taken with him; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 7:20">on the day of the full moon he will enter his house.” <verse eid="PRO 7:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 7:21"/>She turns him aside with the abundance of her speech; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 7:21">with the smoothness of her lips she compels him. <verse eid="PRO 7:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 7:22"/>Going after her suddenly, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 7:22">he goes in like an ox to the slaughter, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 7:22">like a deer bounding into a trap,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7.22 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Probable reading (see LXX, Vulgate, Syriac); Hebrew </char><char style="fq" closed="false">like fetters to discipline a fool</char></note> <verse eid="PRO 7:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 7:23"/>until an arrow splits his liver, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 7:23">like the hurrying of a bird to the snare, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 7:23">and he did not know that it <char style="add">was</char> for his soul! <verse eid="PRO 7:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 7:24"/>And now, sons, listen to me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 7:24">and attend to the words of my mouth. <verse eid="PRO 7:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 7:25"/>Do not let your heart turn aside to her ways, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 7:25">do not stray into her paths. <verse eid="PRO 7:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 7:26"/>For many wounded ones she has made fall; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 7:26">and numerous <char style="add">are</char> all her slain ones. <verse eid="PRO 7:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 7:27"/>Her house <char style="add">is</char> the way to Sheol, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 7:27">going down to the chambers of death. <verse eid="PRO 7:27"/></para>

<chapter eid="PRO 7"/>

<chapter number="8" style="c" sid="PRO 8"/>

<para style="s">The Excellence of Wisdom</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 8:1"/>Does not wisdom cry out, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 8:1">and understanding give forth her voice? <verse eid="PRO 8:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 8:2"/>At the head of the heights, beside the road, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 8:2">at the house of the paths, she takes her stand. <verse eid="PRO 8:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 8:3"/>At the hand of the gates, at the mouth of the city, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 8:3">at the entrance of the doors, she cries out: <verse eid="PRO 8:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 8:4"/>“To you⁺, O men, do I call, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 8:4">and my voice <char style="add">is</char> to the sons of man! <verse eid="PRO 8:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 8:5"/>Discern prudence, O simple ones; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 8:5">and <char style="add">you</char> foolish ones, understand the heart.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">8.5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">instruct your minds</char></note> <verse eid="PRO 8:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 8:6"/>Listen, for noble <char style="add">things</char> do I speak, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 8:6">and the opening of my lips <char style="add">is</char> uprightness. <verse eid="PRO 8:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 8:7"/>For my mouth utters truth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 8:7">and wickedness <char style="add">is</char> an abomination to my lips. <verse eid="PRO 8:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 8:8"/>In righteousness <char style="add">are</char> all the words of my mouth; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 8:8">nothing in them <char style="add">is</char> crooked or perverse. <verse eid="PRO 8:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 8:9"/>All of them <char style="add">are</char> plain to the intelligent, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 8:9">and upright to those finding knowledge. <verse eid="PRO 8:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 8:10"/>Receive my instruction and not silver, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 8:10">and knowledge <char style="add">above</char> choicest gold. <verse eid="PRO 8:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 8:11"/>For better <char style="add">is</char> wisdom than rubies, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 8:11">and all delights cannot be compared with her. <verse eid="PRO 8:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 8:12"/>I, wisdom, dwell with prudence, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 8:12">and knowledge of discretion I find out. <verse eid="PRO 8:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 8:13"/>The fear of YHWH <char style="add">is</char> to hate evil; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 8:13">I hate pride, and arrogance, and the way of evil, and the mouth of perversity. <verse eid="PRO 8:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 8:14"/>Counsel and sound wisdom <char style="add">are</char> unto me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 8:14">I am understanding; unto me <char style="add">is</char> strength. <verse eid="PRO 8:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 8:15"/>By me kings reign, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 8:15">and rulers decree justice. <verse eid="PRO 8:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 8:16"/>By me princes rule, and nobles—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 8:16">all those judging <char style="add">with</char> righteousness.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">8.16 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Some Hebrew manuscripts and LXX </char><char style="fq" closed="false">those governing the earth</char></note> <verse eid="PRO 8:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 8:17"/>I love those who love me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 8:17">and those seeking me earnestly will find me. <verse eid="PRO 8:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 8:18"/>Riches and honor <char style="add">are</char> with me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 8:18">surpassing wealth and righteousness. <verse eid="PRO 8:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 8:19"/>Better <char style="add">is</char> my fruit than gold, even pure gold, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 8:19">and my produce than choice silver. <verse eid="PRO 8:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 8:20"/>In the way of righteousness I walk, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 8:20">in the midst of the paths of justice, <verse eid="PRO 8:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 8:21"/>to cause those loving me to inherit substance, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 8:21">and their treasuries I will fill. <verse eid="PRO 8:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 8:22"/>YHWH acquired me at the beginning of His way,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">8.22 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">YHWH created me as his first course</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 8:22">before His works at that time. <verse eid="PRO 8:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 8:23"/>From everlasting I was poured out, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 8:23">from the head, from before the earth. <verse eid="PRO 8:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 8:24"/>In <char style="add">being</char> no depths, I was brought forth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 8:24">in <char style="add">being</char> no springs heavy with waters. <verse eid="PRO 8:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 8:25"/>Before the mountains were sunk, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 8:25">before the hills, I was brought forth— <verse eid="PRO 8:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 8:26"/>while He had not made the land, or the outside places, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 8:26">or the first dusts of the world. <verse eid="PRO 8:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 8:27"/>In His establishing the heavens, I <char style="add">was</char> there; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 8:27">in His inscribing a circle on the face of the deep, <verse eid="PRO 8:27"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 8:28"/>in His strengthening the clouds above, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 8:28">in His making strong the fountains of the deep, <verse eid="PRO 8:28"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PRO 8:29"/>in His setting for the sea its limit, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 8:29">so that the waters would not cross over His command, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 8:29">in His marking out the foundations of the earth, <verse eid="PRO 8:29"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PRO 8:30"/>then I was beside Him <char style="add">as</char> a craftsman, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 8:30">and I was a delight<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">8.30 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">I was filled with His delight</char></note> day by day, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 8:30">laughing before His face at every time, <verse eid="PRO 8:30"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PRO 8:31"/>laughing in the world of His earth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 8:31">and delighting together with the sons of man. <verse eid="PRO 8:31"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PRO 8:32"/>So now, my sons, listen to me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 8:32">for blessed are those who keep my ways. <verse eid="PRO 8:32"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="PRO 8:33"/>Listen <char style="add">to</char> discipline and be wise, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 8:33">and do not neglect <char style="add">it</char>. <verse eid="PRO 8:33"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="PRO 8:34"/>Blessed <char style="add">is</char> the man listening to me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 8:34">watching at my gates day by day, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 8:34">keeping watch <char style="add">at</char> the posts of my doors. <verse eid="PRO 8:34"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="PRO 8:35"/>For the one finding me has found life, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 8:35">and he brings forth favor from YHWH; <verse eid="PRO 8:35"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="36" style="v" sid="PRO 8:36"/>but the one sinning against me is wronging his soul; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 8:36">all those hating me love death.” <verse eid="PRO 8:36"/></para>

<chapter eid="PRO 8"/>

<chapter number="9" style="c" sid="PRO 9"/>

<para style="s">The Way of Wisdom</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 9:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Proverbs 1:1–7</char></note>Wisdom has built her house; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 9:1">she has hewn out<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">9.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Hebrew; LXX, Syriac, and Aramaic Targum </char><char style="fq" closed="false">she has set up</char></note> her seven pillars. <verse eid="PRO 9:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 9:2"/>She has slaughtered her slaughter; she has mixed her wine; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 9:2">indeed, she has arranged her table. <verse eid="PRO 9:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 9:3"/>She has sent out her maidens; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 9:3">she calls out on the tops of the heights of the city: <verse eid="PRO 9:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 9:4"/>“Who <char style="add">is</char> simple? Let him turn in here!” </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 9:4">To the lacking of heart, she says to him: <verse eid="PRO 9:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 9:5"/>“Come, feed on my bread </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 9:5">and drink the wine I have mixed. <verse eid="PRO 9:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 9:6"/>Forsake foolishness, and live, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 9:6">and walk in the way of understanding.” <verse eid="PRO 9:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 9:7"/>The one correcting one scoffing is receiving for himself shame, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 9:7">and the one rebuking a wicked one, his blemish. <verse eid="PRO 9:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 9:8"/>Do not rebuke one scoffing, lest he hate you; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 9:8">Give reproof to a wise one, and he will love you. <verse eid="PRO 9:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 9:9"/>Give to a wise one, and he will be wiser still; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 9:9">give knowledge to a righteous one, and he will increase in learning. <verse eid="PRO 9:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 9:10"/>The beginning of wisdom <char style="add">is</char> the fear of YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 9:10">and knowledge of the Holy One <char style="add">is</char> understanding. <verse eid="PRO 9:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 9:11"/>For through <char style="add">wisdom</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">9.11 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> LXX, Syriac, and Aramaic Targum; Hebrew </char><char style="fq" closed="false">through me</char></note> your days will be multiplied, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 9:11">and years of life will be added to you. <verse eid="PRO 9:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 9:12"/>If you have been wise, you have been wise for yourself, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 9:12">and <char style="add">if</char> you have scoffed, you will bear <char style="add">it</char> for yourself alone. <verse eid="PRO 9:12"/></para>

<para style="s">The Way of Folly</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 9:13"/>The woman of foolishness roars; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 9:13"><char style="add">she is</char> simple, and she has not known anything. <verse eid="PRO 9:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 9:14"/>And she sits at the door of her house, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 9:14">upon a seat in the heights of the city, <verse eid="PRO 9:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 9:15"/>to call to those passing by the way, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 9:15">those going straight <char style="add">on</char> their paths: <verse eid="PRO 9:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 9:16"/>“Who <char style="add">is</char> simple? Let him turn in here!” </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 9:16">And the lacking of heart, she says to him: <verse eid="PRO 9:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 9:17"/>“Stolen waters are sweet, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 9:17">and bread of secrecies is pleasant.” <verse eid="PRO 9:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 9:18"/>He does not know that the Rephaim<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">9.18 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the dead</char></note> <char style="add">are</char> there; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 9:18">her called ones <char style="add">are</char> in the depths of Sheol. <verse eid="PRO 9:18"/></para>

<chapter eid="PRO 9"/>

<chapter number="10" style="c" sid="PRO 10"/>

<para style="s">Solomon’s Proverbs: The Wise Son</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 10:1"/>The Proverbs of Solomon: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PRO 10:1">A wise son makes a father glad, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 10:1">and a foolish son <char style="add">is</char> the grief of his mother. <verse eid="PRO 10:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 10:2"/>The treasures of wickedness will not bring gain, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 10:2">and righteousness delivers from death. <verse eid="PRO 10:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 10:3"/>YHWH will not let the righteous soul go hungry, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 10:3">and the desire of the wicked ones He thrusts away. <verse eid="PRO 10:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 10:4"/>The one making slack <char style="add">his</char> hand becomes poor, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 10:4">and the hand of the diligent ones makes rich. <verse eid="PRO 10:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 10:5"/>The one gathering in the summer <char style="add">is</char> a wise son; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 10:5">one sleeping in the harvest <char style="add">is</char> a son causing shame. <verse eid="PRO 10:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 10:6"/>Blessings <char style="add">are</char> on the head of the righteous, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 10:6">and the mouth of the wicked conceals violence.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">10.6 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">but violence covers the mouth of the wicked</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; also in verse 11</char></note> <verse eid="PRO 10:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 10:7"/>The memory of the righteous <char style="add">is</char> for a blessing, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 10:7">and the name of the wicked will rot. <verse eid="PRO 10:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 10:8"/>The one wise of heart receives commands, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 10:8">and the one foolish of lips will be thrown down. <verse eid="PRO 10:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 10:9"/>The one walking in integrity walks securely, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 10:9">and the one twisting his ways will be known. <verse eid="PRO 10:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 10:10"/>The one winking with the eye gives grief, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 10:10">and foolish lips will be thrown down.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">10.10 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">babbling fools will fall</char></note> <verse eid="PRO 10:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 10:11"/>A fountain of life <char style="add">is</char> the mouth of a righteous one, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 10:11">and the mouth of the wicked conceals violence. <verse eid="PRO 10:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 10:12"/>Hatred stirs up strife, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 10:12">and love covers over all transgressions. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">10.12 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> See 1 Peter 4:8</char></note><verse eid="PRO 10:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 10:13"/>On the lips of a discerning one wisdom is found, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 10:13">and a rod <char style="add">is</char> for the back of the one lacking understanding. <verse eid="PRO 10:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 10:14"/>The wise treasure knowledge, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 10:14">and the mouth of the fool <char style="add">is</char> near destruction. <verse eid="PRO 10:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 10:15"/>The wealth of a rich one <char style="add">is</char> the city of his strength; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 10:15">the destruction of the poor <char style="add">is</char> their poverty. <verse eid="PRO 10:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 10:16"/>The wage of the righteous <char style="add">is</char> for life; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 10:16">the produce of the wicked <char style="add">is</char> for sin. <verse eid="PRO 10:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 10:17"/>The path to life the one guarding discipline, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 10:17">and one forsaking rebuke goes astray. <verse eid="PRO 10:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 10:18"/>The one covering hatred <char style="add">has</char> lips of falsehood, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 10:18">and the one bringing forth slander, he <char style="add">is</char> a fool. <verse eid="PRO 10:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 10:19"/>In the multitude of words sin is not lacking, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 10:19">and the one restraining his lips <char style="add">is</char> wise. <verse eid="PRO 10:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 10:20"/>The tongue of the righteous <char style="add">is</char> choice silver; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 10:20">the heart of the wicked <char style="add">is</char> for little. <verse eid="PRO 10:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 10:21"/>The lips of the righteous feed many, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 10:21">and fools die by lack of heart. <verse eid="PRO 10:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 10:22"/>The blessing of YHWH—it enriches, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 10:22">and toil cannot add to it. <verse eid="PRO 10:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 10:23"/>The doing of evil <char style="add">is</char> like laughter to a fool, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 10:23">and wisdom <char style="add">is</char> unto a man of understanding. <verse eid="PRO 10:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 10:24"/>The terror of a wicked one—it will come to him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 10:24">and the desire of the righteous is given. <verse eid="PRO 10:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 10:25"/>At the passing over of a whirlwind, a wicked one <char style="add">is</char> no more, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 10:25">and a righteous one <char style="add">has</char> a foundation forever. <verse eid="PRO 10:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 10:26"/>Like vinegar to the teeth and smoke to the eyes, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 10:26">so <char style="add">is</char> the sluggish one to those sending him. <verse eid="PRO 10:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 10:27"/>The fear of YHWH adds days, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 10:27">and the years of the wicked will be short. <verse eid="PRO 10:27"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 10:28"/>The hope of the righteous ones <char style="add">is</char> joy, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 10:28">and the expectation of the wicked ones will perish. <verse eid="PRO 10:28"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PRO 10:29"/>The way of YHWH <char style="add">is</char> strength for the upright, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 10:29">and destruction for doers of iniquity. <verse eid="PRO 10:29"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PRO 10:30"/>A righteous one will not be shaken forever, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 10:30">and the wicked will not dwell in the land. <verse eid="PRO 10:30"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PRO 10:31"/>The mouth of a righteous one brings forth wisdom, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 10:31">and a tongue of perversity will be cut out. <verse eid="PRO 10:31"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PRO 10:32"/>The lips of the righteous know what is pleasing, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 10:32">and the mouth of the wicked ones, perversity. <verse eid="PRO 10:32"/></para>

<chapter eid="PRO 10"/>

<chapter number="11" style="c" sid="PRO 11"/>

<para style="s">Dishonest Scales</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 11:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Ezekiel 45:10–12</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Deuteronomy 25:13–16</char></note>Scales of deceit <char style="add">are</char> an abomination to YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 11:1">and a whole stone <char style="add">is</char> His delight. <verse eid="PRO 11:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 11:2"/>Pride has come, and shame also comes, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 11:2">and with the humble <char style="add">is</char> wisdom. <verse eid="PRO 11:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 11:3"/>The integrity of the upright ones guides them, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 11:3">and the perversity of the treacherous ones destroys them. <verse eid="PRO 11:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 11:4"/>Wealth will not profit in the day of wrath, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 11:4">and righteousness delivers from death. <verse eid="PRO 11:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 11:5"/>The righteousness of a blameless one makes his way straight, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 11:5">and in his wickedness a wicked one will fall. <verse eid="PRO 11:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 11:6"/>The righteousness of the upright ones will deliver them, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 11:6">and by their own desires those acting treacherously are captured. <verse eid="PRO 11:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 11:7"/>With the death of a wicked man, expectation perishes, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 11:7">and the hope of his vigor perishes. <verse eid="PRO 11:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 11:8"/>A righteous one is drawn out from distress, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 11:8">and it comes to the wicked in his place. <verse eid="PRO 11:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 11:9"/>With the mouth a godless one destroys his neighbor, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 11:9">and with knowledge righteous ones will be delivered. <verse eid="PRO 11:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 11:10"/>In the good of the righteous ones a city rejoices, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 11:10">and in the destruction of wicked ones <char style="add">is</char> a shout of joy. <verse eid="PRO 11:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 11:11"/>By the blessing of the upright a city is lifted high, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 11:11">and by the mouth of the wicked ones it is torn down. <verse eid="PRO 11:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 11:12"/>The one despising his neighbor <char style="add">is</char> lacking of heart, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 11:12">and a man of understanding keeps quiet. <verse eid="PRO 11:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 11:13"/>One going about slandering is revealing secret counsel, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 11:13">and the one faithful of spirit conceals the matter. <verse eid="PRO 11:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 11:14"/>Without counsels, a people falls, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 11:14">and salvation <char style="add">is</char> in many giving counsel. <verse eid="PRO 11:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 11:15"/>One will surely suffer evil if he pledges for <char style="add">for</char> a stranger, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 11:15">and one who hates striking hands remains secure. <verse eid="PRO 11:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 11:16"/>A woman of grace grasps honor, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 11:16">and the ruthless ones grasp riches. <verse eid="PRO 11:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 11:17"/>A man of kindness deals well <char style="add">with</char> his soul, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 11:17">and a cruel one troubles his flesh. <verse eid="PRO 11:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 11:18"/>A wicked one makes a reward of deception, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 11:18">and the one sowing righteousness <char style="add">has</char> a wage of truth. <verse eid="PRO 11:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 11:19"/>Rightly <char style="add">is</char> righteousness for life, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 11:19">and the one pursuing evil <char style="add">is</char> unto his own death. <verse eid="PRO 11:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 11:20"/>The crooked of heart are an abomination to YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 11:20">and those blameless in <char style="add">their</char> way <char style="add">are</char> His delight. <verse eid="PRO 11:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 11:21"/>Hand to hand, a wicked one is not acquitted, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 11:21">and the seed of the righteous will escape <char style="add">punishment</char>. <verse eid="PRO 11:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 11:22"/>A ring of gold in the nose of a pig, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 11:22"><char style="add">is</char> a beautiful woman lacking discretion. <verse eid="PRO 11:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 11:23"/>The desire of the righteous <char style="add">is</char> only good, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 11:23">and the hope of the wicked <char style="add">is</char> wrath. <verse eid="PRO 11:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 11:24"/>There is one dispersing, and increasing more, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 11:24">and one withholding from uprightness, only for lack. <verse eid="PRO 11:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 11:25"/>A soul of blessing is made fat, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 11:25">and the one who drenches, he also will sprout. <verse eid="PRO 11:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 11:26"/>The one withholding grain, the people will curse him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 11:26">and blessing <char style="add">is</char> on the head of the one selling. <verse eid="PRO 11:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 11:27"/>The one earnestly seeking good seeks favor, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 11:27">and the one seeking evil, it will come to him. <verse eid="PRO 11:27"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 11:28"/>The one trusting in his riches, he will fall, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 11:28">and the righteous ones will sprout like the leaf. <verse eid="PRO 11:28"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PRO 11:29"/>The one troubling his own house will inherit the wind, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 11:29">and the fool <char style="add">is</char> servant to the wise of heart. <verse eid="PRO 11:29"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PRO 11:30"/>The fruit of a righteous one <char style="add">is</char> a tree of life, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 11:30">and the one taking souls <char style="add">is</char> wise. <verse eid="PRO 11:30"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PRO 11:31"/>Behold, a righteous one will be repaid in the land, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 11:31">surely also the ungodly and the sinner! <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">11.31 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> LXX </char><char style="fq" closed="false">If it is hard for the righteous to be saved, what will become of the ungodly and the sinner?</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Cited in 1 Peter 4:18</char></note><verse eid="PRO 11:31"/></para>

<chapter eid="PRO 11"/>

<chapter number="12" style="c" sid="PRO 12"/>

<para style="s">Loving Discipline and Knowledge</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 12:1"/>The one loving discipline is loving knowledge, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 12:1">and the one hating correction <char style="add">is</char> stupid. <verse eid="PRO 12:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 12:2"/>A good one brings forth favor from YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 12:2">and a man of schemes He will condemn. <verse eid="PRO 12:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 12:3"/>A man is not established by wickedness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 12:3">and the root of the righteous shall not be shaken. <verse eid="PRO 12:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 12:4"/>A woman of virtue <char style="add">is</char> a crown to her husband, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 12:4">and the one causing shame <char style="add">is</char> like rottenness in his bones. <verse eid="PRO 12:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 12:5"/>The thoughts of the righteous ones <char style="add">are</char> justice; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 12:5">the counsels of the wicked ones <char style="add">are for</char> deceit. <verse eid="PRO 12:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 12:6"/>The words of the wicked ones lie in wait <char style="add">for</char> blood, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 12:6">and the mouth of the upright ones delivers them. <verse eid="PRO 12:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 12:7"/>Wicked ones are overthrown, and they are no more, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 12:7">and the house of the righteous ones shall stand. <verse eid="PRO 12:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 12:8"/>A man is praised according to the mouth of his insight, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 12:8">and the one crooked of heart will be for contempt. <verse eid="PRO 12:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 12:9"/>Better to be lightly esteemed, and a servant <char style="add">is</char> unto him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 12:9">than the one honoring himself and lacking bread. <verse eid="PRO 12:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 12:10"/>A righteous one regards the life of his animal, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 12:10">and the mercies of the wicked ones <char style="add">are</char> cruel. <verse eid="PRO 12:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 12:11"/>The one working his land is satisfied <char style="add">with</char> bread, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 12:11">while the one pursuing vanities <char style="add">is</char> lacking of heart. <verse eid="PRO 12:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 12:12"/>The wicked desires the net of evildoers, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 12:12">and the root of the righteous ones will give. <verse eid="PRO 12:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 12:13"/>The snare of a wicked one <char style="add">is</char> in the transgression of lips, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 12:13">and a righteous one will come out from distress. <verse eid="PRO 12:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 12:14"/>From the fruit of the mouth, a man will be satisfied with good, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 12:14">and the recompence of the hands of a man returns to him. <verse eid="PRO 12:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 12:15"/>The way of a fool <char style="add">is</char> right in his own eyes, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 12:15">and the one listening to counsel <char style="add">is</char> wise. <verse eid="PRO 12:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 12:16"/>The fool—in a day his anger is known; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 12:16">and a prudent one covers shame. <verse eid="PRO 12:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 12:17"/>The one breathing forth truth declares righteousness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 12:17">and a witness of falsehoods, deceit. <verse eid="PRO 12:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 12:18"/>There is one speaking rashly like the thrusts of a sword, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 12:18">and the tongue of the wise ones <char style="add">is</char> healing. <verse eid="PRO 12:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 12:19"/>The lip of truth is established forever, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 12:19">and the tongue of deceit for an instant. <verse eid="PRO 12:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 12:20"/>Deception <char style="add">is</char> in the heart of those devising evil, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 12:20">and for those counseling peace <char style="add">is</char> joy. <verse eid="PRO 12:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 12:21"/>Not any iniquity will meet with the righteous one, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 12:21">and the wicked are full of evil. <verse eid="PRO 12:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 12:22"/>An abomination to YHWH <char style="add">are</char> lips of falsehood, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 12:22">and those acting <char style="add">in</char> truth <char style="add">are</char> His delight. <verse eid="PRO 12:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 12:23"/>A prudent man is concealing knowledge, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 12:23">and the heart of stupid ones calls out folly. <verse eid="PRO 12:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 12:24"/>The hand of the diligent ones will rule, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 12:24">and slothfulness will be <char style="add">put</char> to forced labor. <verse eid="PRO 12:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 12:25"/>Anxiety in the heart of man bends <char style="add">him</char> down, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 12:25">and a good word gladdens it. <verse eid="PRO 12:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 12:26"/>A righteous one searches out from his neighbor, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 12:26">and the way of the wicked leads them astray. <verse eid="PRO 12:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 12:27"/>The slothful one does not roast his game, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 12:27">and the wealth of a man <char style="add">is</char> precious for a diligent one. <verse eid="PRO 12:27"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 12:28"/>In the path of righteousness <char style="add">is</char> life, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 12:28">and in <char style="add">its</char> pathway <char style="add">is</char> no death. <verse eid="PRO 12:28"/></para>

<chapter eid="PRO 12"/>

<chapter number="13" style="c" sid="PRO 13"/>

<para style="s">A Father’s Discipline</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 13:1"/>A son <char style="add">is</char> wise <char style="add">by</char> the discipline of his father, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 13:1">and a mocker does not listen to rebuke. <verse eid="PRO 13:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 13:2"/>From the fruit of the mouth a man eats good things, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 13:2">and the soul of the treacherous, violence. <verse eid="PRO 13:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 13:3"/>One guarding his mouth is keeping his soul; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 13:3">one opening his lips, destruction <char style="add">is</char> unto him. <verse eid="PRO 13:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 13:4"/>The soul of a sluggish one is desiring, and <char style="add">has</char> nothing; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 13:4">and the soul of the diligent ones is made fat. <verse eid="PRO 13:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 13:5"/>A righteous one hates a word of falsehood, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 13:5">and a wicked one causes stench and shame. <verse eid="PRO 13:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 13:6"/>Righteousness guards the one of integrity in the way, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 13:6">and wickedness overthrows the sinner. <verse eid="PRO 13:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 13:7"/>There is one making himself rich and <char style="add">having</char> nothing at all, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 13:7">one making himself poor and <char style="add">having</char> abundant wealth. <verse eid="PRO 13:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 13:8"/>His riches <char style="add">are</char> the ransom for the soul of a man, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 13:8">and a poor one has not heard rebuke. <verse eid="PRO 13:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 13:9"/>The light of the righteous rejoices, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 13:9">and the lamp of the wicked is extinguished. <verse eid="PRO 13:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 13:10"/>Only with arrogance does one give forth strife, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 13:10">and wisdom <char style="add">is</char> with the counseled ones. <verse eid="PRO 13:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 13:11"/>Wealth from vanity is diminished, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 13:11">and the one gathering by the hand becomes great. <verse eid="PRO 13:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 13:12"/>Hope deferred weakens the heart, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 13:12">and desire fulfilled <char style="add">is</char> a tree of life. <verse eid="PRO 13:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 13:13"/>The one despising the word is destroyed for it, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 13:13">and the one fearing the command, he will be rewarded. <verse eid="PRO 13:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 13:14"/>The instruction<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">13.14 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">law</char></note> of the wise <char style="add">is</char> a fountain of life, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 13:14">to turn aside from the snares of death. <verse eid="PRO 13:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 13:15"/>Good insight gives favor, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 13:15">and the way of the treacherous <char style="add">is</char> perpetual. <verse eid="PRO 13:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 13:16"/>Every prudent one acts with knowledge, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 13:16">and a fool spreads out folly. <verse eid="PRO 13:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 13:17"/>A wicked messenger falls into evil, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 13:17">and an envoy of faithfulness <char style="add">is</char> healing. <verse eid="PRO 13:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 13:18"/>Poverty and shame <char style="add">are</char> to one disdaining discipline, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 13:18">and the one regarding a rebuke is honored. <verse eid="PRO 13:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 13:19"/>A desire coming to pass is pleasant to the soul, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 13:19">and turning aside from evil <char style="add">is</char> an abomination to fools. <verse eid="PRO 13:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 13:20"/>The one walking with wise ones will become wise, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 13:20">and the one accompanying fools will suffer evil. <verse eid="PRO 13:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 13:21"/>Evil pursues the sinful ones, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 13:21">and goodness will reward the righteous ones. <verse eid="PRO 13:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 13:22"/>A good one leaves an inheritance <char style="add">for</char> the sons of his sons, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 13:22">and the wealth of the sinner is stored up for a righteous one. <verse eid="PRO 13:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 13:23"/>There is much food <char style="add">in</char> the fallow ground of the poor, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 13:23">and it is swept away for lack of justice. <verse eid="PRO 13:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 13:24"/>The one withholding his rod is hating his son, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 13:24">and one loving him diligently seeks him with discipline. <verse eid="PRO 13:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 13:25"/>A righteous one is eating to the satisfaction of his soul, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 13:25">and the belly of the wicked will be lacking. <verse eid="PRO 13:25"/></para>

<chapter eid="PRO 13"/>

<chapter number="14" style="c" sid="PRO 14"/>

<para style="s">The Wise Woman</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 14:1"/>The wisest of women builds her house, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 14:1">and a foolish woman with her own hands tears it down. <verse eid="PRO 14:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 14:2"/>The one walking in his uprightness <char style="add">is</char> fearful of YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 14:2">and the one devious in his ways despises Him. <verse eid="PRO 14:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 14:3"/>In the mouth of a fool <char style="add">is</char> a branch of pride, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 14:3">and the lips of the wise ones guard them. <verse eid="PRO 14:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 14:4"/>With no oxen, the trough <char style="add">is</char> empty, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 14:4">and an abundance of produce <char style="add">is</char> by the strength of an ox. <verse eid="PRO 14:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 14:5"/>A witness of faithfulness does not lie, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 14:5">and a witness of deception breathes out lies. <verse eid="PRO 14:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 14:6"/>A scoffer seeks wisdom, and there is none, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 14:6">and knowledge <char style="add">is</char> easy to the discerning one. <verse eid="PRO 14:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 14:7"/>Depart from in front of a man <char style="add">who is</char> foolish, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 14:7">for you will not know there the lips of knowledge. <verse eid="PRO 14:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 14:8"/>The wisdom of a prudent one <char style="add">is</char> to understand his way, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 14:8">and the folly of fools <char style="add">is</char> deceit. <verse eid="PRO 14:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 14:9"/>Fools mock the guilt offering, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 14:9">and among the upright ones <char style="add">is</char> favor. <verse eid="PRO 14:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 14:10"/>The heart knows the bitterness of its own soul, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 14:10">and in its joy a stranger does not share. <verse eid="PRO 14:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 14:11"/>The house of the wicked ones will be destroyed, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 14:11">and the tent of the upright ones will flourish. <verse eid="PRO 14:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 14:12"/>There is a way right before the face of a man, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 14:12">and its end <char style="add">is</char> the way of death. <verse eid="PRO 14:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 14:13"/>Even in laughter a heart may be pained, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 14:13">and the end of joy <char style="add">is</char> grief. <verse eid="PRO 14:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 14:14"/>The one turning back in heart will be filled from his ways, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 14:14">and a good man, from himself. <verse eid="PRO 14:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 14:15"/>The simple one affirms every word, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 14:15">and the prudent one considers his step. <verse eid="PRO 14:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 14:16"/>A wise one fears<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">14.16 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">fears YHWH</char></note> and turns aside from evil, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 14:16">and a fool is transgressing and is confident. <verse eid="PRO 14:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 14:17"/>One short of nostrils acts <char style="add">with</char> foolishness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 14:17">and a man of schemes is hated. <verse eid="PRO 14:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 14:18"/>The simple ones inherit foolishness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 14:18">and the prudent are crowned with knowledge. <verse eid="PRO 14:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 14:19"/>The evil ones will bow before the face of of good ones, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 14:19">and wicked ones at the gates of the righteous one. <verse eid="PRO 14:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 14:20"/>The poor one is hated even by his neighbor, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 14:20">and those loving the rich one <char style="add">are</char> many. <verse eid="PRO 14:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 14:21"/>The one despising his neighbor sins, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 14:21">and the one showing favor <char style="add">to</char> the poor <char style="add">is</char> blessed. <verse eid="PRO 14:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 14:22"/>Do they not go astray <char style="add">who</char> are planning evil? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 14:22">And loving devotion and truth <char style="add">are</char> unto those planning good. <verse eid="PRO 14:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 14:23"/>In all labor there is profit, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 14:23">and a word of the lips <char style="add">is</char> only to poverty. <verse eid="PRO 14:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 14:24"/>The crown of the wise <char style="add">is</char> their wealth; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 14:24">the folly of fools <char style="add">is</char> folly. <verse eid="PRO 14:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 14:25"/>A witness of truth is delivering souls, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 14:25">and one who breathes out lies <char style="add">is</char> deceitful. <verse eid="PRO 14:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 14:26"/>In the fear of YHWH confidence <char style="add">is</char> strong, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 14:26">and for his sons there is a refuge. <verse eid="PRO 14:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 14:27"/>The fear of YHWH <char style="add">is</char> a fountain of life, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 14:27">to turn aside from the snares of death. <verse eid="PRO 14:27"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 14:28"/>In a multitude of people <char style="add">is</char> the glory of a king, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 14:28">and in a lack of people <char style="add">is</char> the ruin of a prince. <verse eid="PRO 14:28"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PRO 14:29"/>The one slow to anger <char style="add">is</char> great in understanding, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 14:29">and the one short of temper lifts up folly. <verse eid="PRO 14:29"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PRO 14:30"/>A heart of healing <char style="add">is</char> life to the body, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 14:30">and jealousy <char style="add">is</char> rottenness to the bones. <verse eid="PRO 14:30"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PRO 14:31"/>The one oppressing the poor reproaches his Maker, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 14:31">and the one honoring Him shows favor <char style="add">to</char> the needy. <verse eid="PRO 14:31"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PRO 14:32"/>By his evil a wicked one is thrust down, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 14:32">and a righteous one takes refuge in his death. <verse eid="PRO 14:32"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="PRO 14:33"/>In the heart of a discerning one wisdom rests, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 14:33">and within fools she makes herself known.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">14.33 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Hebrew; LXX and Syriac </char><char style="fq" closed="false">but among fools she is not known</char></note> <verse eid="PRO 14:33"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="PRO 14:34"/>Righteousness exalts a nation, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 14:34">and sin <char style="add">is</char> a reproach of peoples. <verse eid="PRO 14:34"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="PRO 14:35"/>The favor of a king <char style="add">is</char> toward a wise servant, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 14:35">and his wrath is to one causing shame. <verse eid="PRO 14:35"/></para>

<chapter eid="PRO 14"/>

<chapter number="15" style="c" sid="PRO 15"/>

<para style="s">A Gentle Answer Turns Away Wrath</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 15:1"/>A tender answer turns away rage, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 15:1">and a word of pain raises up anger. <verse eid="PRO 15:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 15:2"/>The tongue of the wise makes knowledge good, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 15:2">and the mouth of fools pours forth folly. <verse eid="PRO 15:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 15:3"/>The eyes of YHWH <char style="add">are</char> in every place, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 15:3">watching evil ones and good ones. <verse eid="PRO 15:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 15:4"/>A healing tongue <char style="add">is</char> a tree of life, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 15:4">and crookedness in it is a breaking in the spirit. <verse eid="PRO 15:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 15:5"/>A fool despises the discipline of his father, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 15:5">and the one receiving correction is prudent. <verse eid="PRO 15:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 15:6"/><char style="add">In</char> the house of the righteous <char style="add">is</char> much treasure, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 15:6">and in the produce of the wicked <char style="add">is</char> trouble. <verse eid="PRO 15:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 15:7"/>The lips of the wise ones scatter knowledge, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 15:7">and the heart of fools, not so. <verse eid="PRO 15:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 15:8"/>The sacrifice of the wicked ones <char style="add">is</char> an abomination to YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 15:8">and the prayer of the upright ones <char style="add">is</char> His delight. <verse eid="PRO 15:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 15:9"/>An abomination to YHWH <char style="add">is</char> the way of the wicked, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 15:9">and the one pursuing righteousness, He loves. <verse eid="PRO 15:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 15:10"/>Discipline <char style="add">is</char> grievous to the one abandoning the way; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 15:10">one hating correction will die. <verse eid="PRO 15:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 15:11"/>Sheol and Abaddon<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">15.11 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Death and Destruction</char></note> <char style="add">are</char> before of YHWH—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 15:11">and surely the hearts of the sons of men! <verse eid="PRO 15:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 15:12"/>One mocking does not love one who rebukes to him; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 15:12">he will not go to the wise ones. <verse eid="PRO 15:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 15:13"/>A joyful heart makes a face good, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 15:13">and by sorrow of heart a spirit <char style="add">is</char> stricken. <verse eid="PRO 15:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 15:14"/>A discerning heart seeks knowledge, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 15:14">and the mouth of fools feeds on folly. <verse eid="PRO 15:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 15:15"/>All the days of the afflicted <char style="add">are</char> evil, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 15:15">and a good heart <char style="add">is</char> a continual feast. <verse eid="PRO 15:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 15:16"/>Better <char style="add">is</char> a little with the fear of YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 15:16">than great treasure and anxiety with it. <verse eid="PRO 15:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 15:17"/>Better <char style="add">is</char> a portion of herbs when love <char style="add">is</char> there, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 15:17">than a fattened calf when hatred <char style="add">is</char> with it. <verse eid="PRO 15:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 15:18"/>A man of wrath stirs up strife, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 15:18">and one long of nostrils quiets fighting. <verse eid="PRO 15:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 15:19"/>The way of the sluggish one <char style="add">is</char> like a hedge of thorns, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 15:19">and the path of the upright is raised up. <verse eid="PRO 15:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 15:20"/>A wise son gladdens <char style="add">his</char> father, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 15:20">and a foolish man despises his mother. <verse eid="PRO 15:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 15:21"/>Folly <char style="add">is</char> joy to the one lacking heart, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 15:21">and a man of understanding makes straight <char style="add">his</char> walk. <verse eid="PRO 15:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 15:22"/>Plans without counsel are broken, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 15:22">and in a multitude of counselors it is established. <verse eid="PRO 15:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 15:23"/>Joy <char style="add">is</char> unto a man in the answer of his mouth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 15:23">and a word in its season, how good <char style="add">it is</char>! <verse eid="PRO 15:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 15:24"/>The path of life <char style="add">is</char> on high for the one being wise, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 15:24">that he may turn away from Sheol below. <verse eid="PRO 15:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 15:25"/>YHWH will tear down the house of the proud ones, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 15:25">and He will make stand the boundary of the widow. <verse eid="PRO 15:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 15:26"/>An abomination YHWH <char style="add">are</char> the thoughts of the wicked, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 15:26">and pure <char style="add">are</char> words of pleasantness. <verse eid="PRO 15:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 15:27"/>The one being greedy for dishonest gain is troubling his house, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 15:27">and the one hating bribes will live. <verse eid="PRO 15:27"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 15:28"/>The heart of the righteous ponders <char style="add">how</char> to answer, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 15:28">and the mouth of the wicked pours forth evils. <verse eid="PRO 15:28"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PRO 15:29"/>Far <char style="add">is</char> YHWH from the wicked, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 15:29">and He hears the prayer of the righteous. <verse eid="PRO 15:29"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PRO 15:30"/>The light of the eyes gladdens the heart; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 15:30">a good report fattens the bone. <verse eid="PRO 15:30"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PRO 15:31"/>The ear hearing the rebukes of life, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 15:31">it will abide among the wise ones. <verse eid="PRO 15:31"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PRO 15:32"/>The one neglecting discipline despises his own soul, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 15:32">and the one hearing a rebuke acquires understanding. <verse eid="PRO 15:32"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="PRO 15:33"/>The fear of YHWH <char style="add">is</char> the instruction of wisdom, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 15:33">and before the face of honor <char style="add">is</char> humility. <verse eid="PRO 15:33"/></para>

<chapter eid="PRO 15"/>

<chapter number="16" style="c" sid="PRO 16"/>

<para style="s">The Reply of the Tongue Is from Yahweh</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 16:1"/>The plans of the heart <char style="add">are</char> unto man, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 16:1">and from YHWH <char style="add">is</char> the answer of the tongue. <verse eid="PRO 16:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 16:2"/>All the ways of a man <char style="add">are</char> pure in his own eyes, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 16:2">and YHWH weighs out the spirit. <verse eid="PRO 16:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 16:3"/>Roll your works toward YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 16:3">and your plans will be established. <verse eid="PRO 16:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 16:4"/>YHWH has made everything for its own end—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 16:4">even the wicked for the day of evil. <verse eid="PRO 16:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 16:5"/>An abomination to YHWH <char style="add">is</char> everyone high of heart; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 16:5">hand to hand, he will not be acquitted. <verse eid="PRO 16:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 16:6"/>By loving devotion and faithfulness iniquity is atoned for, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 16:6">and by the fear of YHWH one turns aside from evil. <verse eid="PRO 16:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 16:7"/>When the ways of a man please YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 16:7">He makes even his enemies to be at peace with him. <verse eid="PRO 16:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 16:8"/>Better <char style="add">is</char> a little with righteousness </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 16:8">than an abundance of increase without justice. <verse eid="PRO 16:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 16:9"/>The heart of man plans his way, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 16:9">and YHWH establishes his step. <verse eid="PRO 16:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 16:10"/>Divination <char style="add">is</char> on the lips of the king; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 16:10">in judgment his mouth shall not be unfaithful. <verse eid="PRO 16:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 16:11"/>A balance and scales of justice <char style="add">are</char> unto YHWH; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 16:11">all the stones of the bag <char style="add">are</char> His work. <verse eid="PRO 16:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 16:12"/>An abomination to kings is to commit wickedness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 16:12">for by righteousness a throne is established. <verse eid="PRO 16:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 16:13"/>Lips of righteousness <char style="add">are</char> the delight of kings, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 16:13">and one speaking uprightly he loves. <verse eid="PRO 16:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 16:14"/>The wrath of a king <char style="add">is as</char> messengers of death, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 16:14">and a wise man will appease it. <verse eid="PRO 16:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 16:15"/>In the light of the face of a king <char style="add">is</char> life, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 16:15">and his favor <char style="add">is</char> like a cloud of spring rain. <verse eid="PRO 16:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 16:16"/>To acquire wisdom—how much better than gold! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 16:16">And to acquire understanding <char style="add">is</char> to be chosen above silver! <verse eid="PRO 16:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 16:17"/>The highway of the upright ones turns aside from evil; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 16:17">one guarding his soul watches over his way. <verse eid="PRO 16:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 16:18"/>Before the face of breaking <char style="add">is</char> pride, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 16:18">and before a fall <char style="add">is</char> a haughty spirit. <verse eid="PRO 16:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 16:19"/>Better to be lowly spirit among the poor, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 16:19">than to divide plunder with proud ones. <verse eid="PRO 16:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 16:20"/>One acting wisely concerning a matter will find good,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">16.20 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Whoever speaks prudently will find what is good</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 16:20">and one trusting in YHWH <char style="add">is</char> blessed. <verse eid="PRO 16:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 16:21"/>The one wise of heart is called discerning, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 16:21">and sweetness of lips increases learning. <verse eid="PRO 16:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 16:22"/>A fountain of life <char style="add">is</char> understanding to its owners, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 16:22">and the discipline of fools <char style="add">is</char> folly. <verse eid="PRO 16:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 16:23"/>The heart of the wise causes his mouth to act wisely, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 16:23">and upon his lips he increases learning. <verse eid="PRO 16:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 16:24"/>Words of pleasantness <char style="add">are</char> a comb of honey—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 16:24">sweet to the soul and healing to the bone. <verse eid="PRO 16:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 16:25"/>There is a way right before the face of a man, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 16:25">and its end is the way of death. <verse eid="PRO 16:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 16:26"/>The soul of the laborer labors for himself, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 16:26">because his mouth presses him onward. <verse eid="PRO 16:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 16:27"/>A man of worthlessness digs up evil, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 16:27">and upon his lips <char style="add">it is</char> like a fire burning. <verse eid="PRO 16:27"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 16:28"/>A man of perversity sends out strife, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 16:28">and a murmurer is separating a close friend. <verse eid="PRO 16:28"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PRO 16:29"/>A man of violence entices his neighbor </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 16:29">and leads him in a way <char style="add">that is</char> not good. <verse eid="PRO 16:29"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PRO 16:30"/>Winking his eyes to devise perversity, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 16:30">pursing his lips, he has accomplished evil. <verse eid="PRO 16:30"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PRO 16:31"/>Grey hair <char style="add">is</char> a crown of glory; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 16:31">along the path of righteousness it is found. <verse eid="PRO 16:31"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PRO 16:32"/>Better <char style="add">is</char> one slow to anger than a mighty one, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 16:32">and one ruling over his spirit than one taking a city. <verse eid="PRO 16:32"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="PRO 16:33"/>Into the lap the lot is cast, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 16:33">and all its judgment <char style="add">is</char> from YHWH. <verse eid="PRO 16:33"/></para>

<chapter eid="PRO 16"/>

<chapter number="17" style="c" sid="PRO 17"/>

<para style="s">Better a Dry Morsel in Quietness</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 17:1"/>Better <char style="add">is</char> a dry morsel and quietness with it, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 17:1">than a house full of feasting<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">17.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">sacrifices</char></note> with strife. <verse eid="PRO 17:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 17:2"/>A wise servant rules over a son who acts shamefully, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 17:2">and in the midst of brothers he will share an inheritance. <verse eid="PRO 17:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 17:3"/>The crucible <char style="add">is</char> for silver and the furnace for gold, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 17:3">and the One testing hearts <char style="add">is</char> YHWH. <verse eid="PRO 17:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 17:4"/>One doing evil pays attention to lips of iniquity; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 17:4">a liar gives ear to a tongue of evil desires. <verse eid="PRO 17:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 17:5"/>One mocking the poor scorns his Maker; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 17:5">one glad at calamity will not be acquitted. <verse eid="PRO 17:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 17:6"/>The crown of old men <char style="add">are</char> the sons of sons, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 17:6">and the glory of sons <char style="add">are</char> their fathers. <verse eid="PRO 17:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 17:7"/>A lip of excellence is not lovely to a fool, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 17:7">even less to a prince <char style="add">is</char> a lip of falsehood. <verse eid="PRO 17:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 17:8"/>A stone of favor <char style="add">is</char> a bribe in the eyes of its owners—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 17:8">to all that he turns, he prospers. <verse eid="PRO 17:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 17:9"/>The one covering a transgression is seeking love, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 17:9">and one repeating a word is separating a close friend. <verse eid="PRO 17:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 17:10"/>A rebuke goes down into an understanding one, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 17:10">more than a hundred stripes into a fool. <verse eid="PRO 17:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 17:11"/>An evil one seeks only rebellion, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 17:11">and a cruel messenger will be sent against him. <verse eid="PRO 17:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 17:12"/>Let meet a bear robbed of her cubs with a man, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 17:12">and not a fool in his folly. <verse eid="PRO 17:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 17:13"/>One returning evil in exchange for good—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 17:13">evil shall not depart from his house. <verse eid="PRO 17:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 17:14"/>The beginning of strife <char style="add">is</char> a letting out of waters, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 17:14">and before it breaks out, abandon the dispute. <verse eid="PRO 17:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 17:15"/>One justifying the wicked, and condemning the just—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 17:15">even the two of them <char style="add">are</char> an abomination to YHWH. <verse eid="PRO 17:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 17:16"/>Why <char style="add">is</char> <char style="add">is</char> this a payment in the hand of a fool, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 17:16">to buy wisdom without a heart? <verse eid="PRO 17:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 17:17"/>At every time a friend is loving, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 17:17">and a brother is born for distress. <verse eid="PRO 17:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 17:18"/>A man lacking heart is one striking hands, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 17:18">pledging a pledge before the face of his friend. <verse eid="PRO 17:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 17:19"/>The one loving transgression loves strife; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 17:19">the one making high his entrance is seeking destruction. <verse eid="PRO 17:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 17:20"/>The twisted of heart shall not find good, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 17:20">and the turned in his tongue falls into evil. <verse eid="PRO 17:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 17:21"/>The one begetting a fool, grief <char style="add">is</char> unto him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 17:21">and the father of a fool is not glad. <verse eid="PRO 17:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 17:22"/>A joyful heart is good healing, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 17:22">and a spirit stricken dries up the bones. <verse eid="PRO 17:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 17:23"/>A wicked one takes a bribe from the bosom<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">17.23 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">a covert bribe</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 17:23">to stretch aside the paths of justice. <verse eid="PRO 17:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 17:24"/>With the face of a discerning one <char style="add">is</char> wisdom </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 17:24">and the eyes of a fool <char style="add">are</char> at the end of the earth. <verse eid="PRO 17:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 17:25"/>A foolish son <char style="add">is</char> a grief to his father, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 17:25">and bitterness to her who bore him. <verse eid="PRO 17:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 17:26"/>Surely to fine the righteous <char style="add">is</char> not good, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 17:26">to strike nobles for uprightness. <verse eid="PRO 17:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 17:27"/>The one restraining his words <char style="add">is</char> one knowing knowledge, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 17:27"><char style="add">and</char> calm of spirit <char style="add">is</char> a man of understanding. <verse eid="PRO 17:27"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 17:28"/>Even a fool keeping silent is considered wise, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 17:28">one shutting his lips discerning. <verse eid="PRO 17:28"/></para>

<chapter eid="PRO 17"/>

<chapter number="18" style="c" sid="PRO 18"/>

<para style="s">The Selfishness of the Unfriendly</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 18:1"/>The one separating himself seeks his own desire, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 18:1">against all sound wisdom he breaks out. <verse eid="PRO 18:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 18:2"/>A fool does not delight in understanding, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 18:2">but rather in uncovering his heart. <verse eid="PRO 18:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 18:3"/>With the coming of the wicked also comes contempt, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 18:3">and with shame, reproach. <verse eid="PRO 18:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 18:4"/>The words of the mouth of a man <char style="add">are</char> deep waters; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 18:4">the fountain of wisdom <char style="add">is</char> a flowing brook. <verse eid="PRO 18:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 18:5"/>To lift up the face<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">18.5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">To show partiality</char></note> to a wicked one <char style="add">is</char> not good—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 18:5">to overthrow a righteous one in the judgment. <verse eid="PRO 18:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 18:6"/>The lips of a fool enter into strife, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 18:6">and his mouth calls for blows. <verse eid="PRO 18:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 18:7"/>The mouth of a fool <char style="add">is</char> ruin to him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 18:7">and his lips <char style="add">are</char> a snare to his soul. <verse eid="PRO 18:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 18:8"/>The words of a whisperer <char style="add">are</char> like things to be gulped, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 18:8">and they go down into the chambers of the belly. <verse eid="PRO 18:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 18:9"/>The one being slack in his work, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 18:9">he <char style="add">is</char> also a brother to a lord of destruction. <verse eid="PRO 18:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 18:10"/>A tower of strength <char style="add">is</char> the name of YHWH—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 18:10">to it<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">18.10 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">to Him</char></note> a righteous one runs and is set on high. <verse eid="PRO 18:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 18:11"/>The wealth of the rich one <char style="add">is</char> the city of his strength, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 18:11">and like a wall set high in his imagination. <verse eid="PRO 18:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 18:12"/>Before the face of destruction, the heart of a man is exalted, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 18:12">and before honor <char style="add">is</char> humility. <verse eid="PRO 18:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 18:13"/>The one returning a word before he hears, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 18:13">it <char style="add">is</char> folly to him and disgrace. <verse eid="PRO 18:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 18:14"/>The spirit of a man will sustain him in his sickness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 18:14">and a stricken spirit—who can bear it? <verse eid="PRO 18:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 18:15"/>The heart of an understanding one acquires knowledge, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 18:15">and the ear of the wise ones seeks knowledge. <verse eid="PRO 18:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 18:16"/>The gift of a man makes room for him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 18:16">and it leads him before the face of great ones. <verse eid="PRO 18:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 18:17"/>The first in his dispute <char style="add">seems</char> right, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 18:17">until his neighbor comes and examines him. <verse eid="PRO 18:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 18:18"/>The lot makes quarrels cease, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 18:18">and it separates between mighty ones. <verse eid="PRO 18:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 18:19"/>A brother transgressed <char style="add">is</char> as a city of strength, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 18:19">and quarrels <char style="add">are</char> like the gate bar of a citadel. <verse eid="PRO 18:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 18:20"/>From the fruit of the mouth of a man, his belly is satisfied; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 18:20">with the produce of his lips he is satisfied. <verse eid="PRO 18:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 18:21"/>Death and life <char style="add">are</char> in the hand of the tongue, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 18:21">and those loving it will eat its fruit. <verse eid="PRO 18:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 18:22"/>He who has found a wife has found good, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 18:22">and he obtains favor from YHWH. <verse eid="PRO 18:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 18:23"/><char style="add">With</char> supplications the poor one speaks, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 18:23">and a rich one answers fiercely. <verse eid="PRO 18:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 18:24"/>A man of companions may come to ruin, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 18:24">and there is a lover adhering more than a brother. <verse eid="PRO 18:24"/></para>

<chapter eid="PRO 18"/>

<chapter number="19" style="c" sid="PRO 19"/>

<para style="s">The Man of Integrity</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 19:1"/>Better <char style="add">is</char> one being poor walking in his integrity </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 19:1">than the one crooked <char style="add">in</char> his lips, and he <char style="add">is</char> a fool. <verse eid="PRO 19:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 19:2"/>Also, a soul without knowledge <char style="add">is</char> not good; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 19:2">and the one hurrying with <char style="add">his</char> feet is sinning. <verse eid="PRO 19:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 19:3"/>The folly of a man perverts his way, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 19:3">and his heart rages against YHWH. <verse eid="PRO 19:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 19:4"/>Wealth adds many friends, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 19:4">and a poor one is separated from his friend. <verse eid="PRO 19:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 19:5"/>A witness of falsehoods will not be acquitted, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 19:5">and the one breathing out lies will not escape. <verse eid="PRO 19:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 19:6"/>Many will entreat the face of a noble, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 19:6">and everyone <char style="add">is</char> the friend to a man of gift. <verse eid="PRO 19:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 19:7"/>All the brothers of a poor one hate him; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 19:7">surely also his friends are far from him! </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PRO 19:7">He pursues with words—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 19:7">they are nowhere. <verse eid="PRO 19:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 19:8"/>The one acquiring heart is loving his soul; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 19:8">the one guarding understanding will find good. <verse eid="PRO 19:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 19:9"/>A witness of falsehoods will not be acquitted, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 19:9">and the one breathing out lies will perish. <verse eid="PRO 19:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 19:10"/>Luxury <char style="add">is</char> not fitting for a fool—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 19:10">even less for a slave to rule over princes. <verse eid="PRO 19:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 19:11"/>The discretion of a man makes long his nose, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 19:11">and his splendor is to pass over a transgression. <verse eid="PRO 19:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 19:12"/>The rage of a king <char style="add">is</char> like the roaring of the young lion, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 19:12">and his favor <char style="add">is</char> like dew on the grass. <verse eid="PRO 19:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 19:13"/>A foolish son <char style="add">is</char> the ruin of his father, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 19:13">and the quarrels of a wife <char style="add">are</char> a continual dripping. <verse eid="PRO 19:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 19:14"/>A house and wealth <char style="add">are</char> the inheritance of fathers, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 19:14">and from YHWH <char style="add">is</char> a wife <char style="add">who</char> is prudent. <verse eid="PRO 19:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 19:15"/>Sluggishness causes a deep sleep to fall, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 19:15">and a soul of slackness will be hungry. <verse eid="PRO 19:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 19:16"/>One guarding a commandment is guarding his soul; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 19:16">one despising His ways will die. <verse eid="PRO 19:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 19:17"/>The one showing favor <char style="add">to</char> the poor <char style="add">is</char> lending <char style="add">to</char> YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 19:17">and his dealing He will repay to him. <verse eid="PRO 19:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 19:18"/>Discipline your son, for there is hope, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 19:18">and do not lift up your soul toward putting him to death. <verse eid="PRO 19:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 19:19"/>One harsh of anger lifts up the penalty; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 19:19">indeed, if you deliver <char style="add">him</char>, you will add yet again. <verse eid="PRO 19:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 19:20"/>Listen to counsel and receive discipline, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 19:20">so that you may be wise in your latter end. <verse eid="PRO 19:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 19:21"/>Many plans <char style="add">are</char> in the heart of a man, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 19:21">and the counsel of YHWH, it will stand. <verse eid="PRO 19:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 19:22"/>The desire of a man is loving devotion, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 19:22">and one being poor <char style="add">is</char> better than a man of lies. <verse eid="PRO 19:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 19:23"/>The fear of YHWH <char style="add">is</char> to life, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 19:23">and satisfied he will abide; he will not be visited <char style="add">by</char> evil. <verse eid="PRO 19:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 19:24"/>A lazy one hides his hand in the dish; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 19:24">even to his mouth he will not bring it back. <verse eid="PRO 19:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 19:25"/>Strike a mocker and a simple one acts prudently; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 19:25">and rebuke a discerning one—he will discern knowledge. <verse eid="PRO 19:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 19:26"/>One assaulting a father causes a mother to flee; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 19:26"><char style="add">he is</char> a son causing shame and bringing reproach. <verse eid="PRO 19:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 19:27"/>Cease, my son, to hear instruction—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 19:27">you will stray from the words of knowledge. <verse eid="PRO 19:27"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 19:28"/>A witness of worthlessness scorns justice, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 19:28">and the mouth of wicked ones swallows iniquity. <verse eid="PRO 19:28"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PRO 19:29"/>Judgments are prepared for the mockers, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 19:29">and beatings for the back of fools. <verse eid="PRO 19:29"/></para>

<chapter eid="PRO 19"/>

<chapter number="20" style="c" sid="PRO 20"/>

<para style="s">Wine Is a Mocker</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 20:1"/>Wine <char style="add">is</char> a mocker, strong drink a brawler, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 20:1">and anyone led astray by it is not wise. <verse eid="PRO 20:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 20:2"/>The terror of a king <char style="add">is</char> like the roaring of the young lion; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 20:2">the one making him angry is wronging his own soul.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">20.2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">is forfeiting his life</char></note> <verse eid="PRO 20:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 20:3"/>An honor to a man is cessation from strife, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 20:3">and every fool will quarrel. <verse eid="PRO 20:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 20:4"/>From autumn a lazy one will not will plow, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 20:4">and he begs in the harvest, and <char style="add">there is</char> nothing. <verse eid="PRO 20:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 20:5"/>Counsel in the heart of man <char style="add">is</char> deep waters, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 20:5">and a man of understanding will draw it out. <verse eid="PRO 20:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 20:6"/>Many a man proclaims, each man his loving devotion—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 20:6">and a man of faithfulness, who can find? <verse eid="PRO 20:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 20:7"/>A righteous one is walking about in his integrity; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 20:7">blessed <char style="add">are</char> his sons after him. <verse eid="PRO 20:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 20:8"/>A king sitting on the throne of judgment </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 20:8">is scattering all evil with his eyes. <verse eid="PRO 20:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 20:9"/>Who can say, “I have made clean my heart; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 20:9">I have been cleansed from my sin? <verse eid="PRO 20:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 20:10"/>A stone and a stone, an ephah and an ephah<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">20.10 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Unequal weights and unequal measures</char></note>—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 20:10">the two of them alike <char style="add">are</char> an abomination to YHWH. <verse eid="PRO 20:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 20:11"/>Even by his deeds a child is known, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 20:11">whether his action <char style="add">is</char> pure and upright. <verse eid="PRO 20:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 20:12"/>The ear hearing, and the eye seeing—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 20:12">YHWH has made even both of them. <verse eid="PRO 20:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 20:13"/>You should not love sleep, lest you be dispossessed; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 20:13">open your eyes, be satisfied <char style="add">with</char> bread. <verse eid="PRO 20:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 20:14"/>“Bad, bad,” says the one buying, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 20:14">and having gone away himself, then he boasts. <verse eid="PRO 20:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 20:15"/>There is gold and an abundance of rubies, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 20:15">and the lips of knowledge <char style="add">are</char> a precious vessel. <verse eid="PRO 20:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 20:16"/>Take his garment when it has been pledged for a stranger, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 20:16">and hold it in pledge for a foreign woman.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">20.16 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">a wayward woman</char></note> <verse eid="PRO 20:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 20:17"/>The bread of deceit <char style="add">is</char> sweet to a man, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 20:17">and afterward his mouth will be filled with gravel. <verse eid="PRO 20:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 20:18"/>Plans are established by counsel, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 20:18">and by guidance wage war. <verse eid="PRO 20:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 20:19"/>The one going about <char style="add">with</char> slander uncovers a secret; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 20:19">and do not pledge yourself to the one opening his lips.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">20.19 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">to the one who babbles with his lips</char></note> <verse eid="PRO 20:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 20:20"/>One belittling his father or his mother, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 20:20">his lamp will be extinguished in the pupil of darkness. <verse eid="PRO 20:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 20:21"/>An inheritance gained unjustly at first, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 20:21">even its latter end will not be blessed. <verse eid="PRO 20:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 20:22"/>You should not say, “I will repay evil.” </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 20:22">Wait for YHWH, and He will save you. <verse eid="PRO 20:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 20:23"/>An abomination to YHWH <char style="add">are</char> a stone and a stone, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 20:23">and scales of deceit <char style="add">are</char> not good. <verse eid="PRO 20:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 20:24"/><char style="add">From</char> YHWH <char style="add">are</char> the steps of man; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 20:24">and how can a man understand his way? <verse eid="PRO 20:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 20:25"/><char style="add">It is</char> a snare for a man to rashly declare “It is holy” </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 20:25">and afterward to reconsider <char style="add">his</char> vows. <verse eid="PRO 20:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 20:26"/>Wise <char style="add">is</char> a king scattering the wicked—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 20:26">he even turns the wheel over them. <verse eid="PRO 20:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 20:27"/>The spirit<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">20.27 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">breath</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">speech</char></note> of a man <char style="add">is</char> the lamp of YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 20:27">searching all the chambers of the belly. <verse eid="PRO 20:27"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 20:28"/>Loving devotion and faithfulness guard a king, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 20:28">and his throne is supported by loving devotion. <verse eid="PRO 20:28"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PRO 20:29"/>The glory of young men <char style="add">is</char> their strength, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 20:29">and the splendor of old men, grey hair. <verse eid="PRO 20:29"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PRO 20:30"/>Stripes that wound scour evil, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 20:30">and beatings, the chambers of the belly. <verse eid="PRO 20:30"/></para>

<chapter eid="PRO 20"/>

<chapter number="21" style="c" sid="PRO 21"/>

<para style="s">The King’s Heart</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 21:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Psalm 21:1–13</char></note>Channels of water <char style="add">is</char> the heart of a king in the hand of YHWH; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 21:1">upon all that He wishes, He stretches it out. <verse eid="PRO 21:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 21:2"/>Every way of a man <char style="add">is</char> right in his own eyes, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 21:2">and YHWH is measuring hearts. <verse eid="PRO 21:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 21:3"/>To do righteousness and justice </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 21:3">is chosen of YHWH above sacrifice. <verse eid="PRO 21:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 21:4"/>Loftiness of eyes and broadness of heart—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 21:4">the guides of the wicked—<char style="add">are</char> sin. <verse eid="PRO 21:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 21:5"/>The plans of the diligent <char style="add">are</char> surely to abundance, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 21:5">and everyone hurrying about, surely to poverty. <verse eid="PRO 21:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 21:6"/>Working <char style="add">for</char> treasures by a tongue of deception </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 21:6">is a vapor driven away <char style="add">of those</char> seeking death. <verse eid="PRO 21:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 21:7"/>The violence of the wicked will drag them away, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 21:7">for they refuse to do justice. <verse eid="PRO 21:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 21:8"/>The way of a guilty man <char style="add">is</char> crooked, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 21:8">and <char style="add">for</char> a pure one, his work <char style="add">is</char> straight. <verse eid="PRO 21:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 21:9"/>Better to sit on the corner of a roof, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 21:9">than with a woman of quarrels and a house of company. <verse eid="PRO 21:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 21:10"/>The soul of a wicked one desires evil; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 21:10">his neighbor shall not find favor in his eyes. <verse eid="PRO 21:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 21:11"/>By fining a mocker, a simple one is made wise; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 21:11">and in giving understanding to a wise one, he receives knowledge. <verse eid="PRO 21:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 21:12"/>The Righteous One<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">21.12 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">The righteous one</char></note> considers the house of the wicked, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 21:12">overthrowing the wicked for wickedness. <verse eid="PRO 21:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 21:13"/>One shutting his ears to the cry of the poor, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 21:13">he also will cry out, and will not be answered. <verse eid="PRO 21:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 21:14"/>A gift in secret subdues anger, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 21:14">and a bribe in the bosom,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">21.14 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">a covert bribe</char></note> strong rage. <verse eid="PRO 21:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 21:15"/>A joy for the righteous is doing justice, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 21:15">and a terror for the workers of iniquity. <verse eid="PRO 21:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 21:16"/>A man wandering from the way of understanding </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 21:16">will come to rest in the assembly of Rephaim. <verse eid="PRO 21:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 21:17"/>The one loving pleasure <char style="add">is</char> a man of need, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 21:17">the one loving wine and oil will not become rich. <verse eid="PRO 21:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 21:18"/>A wicked one <char style="add">is</char> a ransom for a righteous one, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 21:18">and the one acting treacherously for upright ones. <verse eid="PRO 21:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 21:19"/>Better to dwell in a land of wilderness </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 21:19">than with a woman of quarrels and provocation. <verse eid="PRO 21:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 21:20"/>Treasure to be desired and oil <char style="add">are</char> in the dwelling of a wise one, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 21:20">and a foolish man swallows it up. <verse eid="PRO 21:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 21:21"/>One pursuing righteousness and loving devotion </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 21:21">will find life, righteousness, and honor. <verse eid="PRO 21:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 21:22"/>A wise one ascends a city of mighty ones, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 21:22">and he brings down the stronghold of its confidence. <verse eid="PRO 21:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 21:23"/>The one guarding his mouth and his tongue </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 21:23">is guarding his soul from distress. <verse eid="PRO 21:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 21:24"/>The arrogant <char style="add">and</char> haughty one—Mocker <char style="add">is</char> his name—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 21:24">he is acting in the outpouring of pride. <verse eid="PRO 21:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 21:25"/>The desire of the lazy one brings him death, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 21:25">for his hands refuse to work. <verse eid="PRO 21:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 21:26"/>All the day he has desired <char style="add">his</char> desire </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 21:26">and the righteous one gives and does not withhold. <verse eid="PRO 21:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 21:27"/>The sacrifice of wicked ones <char style="add">is</char> an abomination—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 21:27">how much more when he brings it in wickedness! <verse eid="PRO 21:27"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 21:28"/>A witness of falsehood will perish, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 21:28">and the man being attentive will speak forever. <verse eid="PRO 21:28"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PRO 21:29"/>A wicked man strengthens his face,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">21.29 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">puts up a bold front</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 21:29">and an upright one—he establishes his way. <verse eid="PRO 21:29"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PRO 21:30"/>There is no wisdom and no understanding </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 21:30">and no counsel against YHWH. <verse eid="PRO 21:30"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PRO 21:31"/>The horse <char style="add">is</char> prepared for the day of battle, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 21:31">and the victory <char style="add">is</char> of YHWH. <verse eid="PRO 21:31"/></para>

<chapter eid="PRO 21"/>

<chapter number="22" style="c" sid="PRO 22"/>

<para style="s">A Good Name</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 22:1"/>A name to be chosen <char style="add">is</char> greater than wealth; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 22:1">favor is better than silver and gold. <verse eid="PRO 22:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 22:2"/>The rich and the poor meet together; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 22:2">the maker of them all <char style="add">is</char> YHWH. <verse eid="PRO 22:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 22:3"/>A prudent one sees evil and hides himself, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 22:3">and the simple ones pass on and they are fined. <verse eid="PRO 22:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 22:4"/>The result of humility <char style="add">and</char> the fear of YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 22:4"><char style="add">is</char> wealth and honor and life. <verse eid="PRO 22:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 22:5"/>Thorns <char style="add">and</char> snares <char style="add">are</char> in the way of the crooked; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 22:5">one guarding his soul will be far from them. <verse eid="PRO 22:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 22:6"/>Train up a child according to the mouth of his way, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 22:6">and when he grows old, he will not turn aside from it. <verse eid="PRO 22:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 22:7"/>A rich one rules over the poor, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 22:7">and one borrowing <char style="add">is</char> a servant to the man lending. <verse eid="PRO 22:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 22:8"/>The one sowing injustice will reap trouble, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 22:8">and the rod of his anger will come to an end. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">22.8 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> LXX includes </char><char style="fq" closed="false">God blesses a cheerful and generous man, but foolish works will come to an end</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; see also 2 Corinthians 9:7.</char></note><verse eid="PRO 22:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 22:9"/>The one good of eye—he will be blessed, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 22:9">for he gives from his bread to the lowly one. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">22.9 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">The generouse one</char></note><verse eid="PRO 22:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 22:10"/>Drive out the one mocking, and quarreling will go out, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 22:10">and strife and shame will cease. <verse eid="PRO 22:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 22:11"/>One loving a pure heart, <char style="add">with</char> favor on his lips, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 22:11">the king <char style="add">is</char> his friend. <verse eid="PRO 22:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 22:12"/>The eyes of YHWH guard knowledge, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 22:12">and He twists the words of a treacherous one. <verse eid="PRO 22:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 22:13"/>A lazy one says, “A lion is outside! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 22:13">In the midst of the open areas I will be killed!” <verse eid="PRO 22:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 22:14"/>The mouth of strange women <char style="add">is</char> a deep pit; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 22:14">the abhorred of YHWH will fall there. <verse eid="PRO 22:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 22:15"/>Foolishness <char style="add">is</char> bound up in the heart of a child; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 22:15">the rod of discipline drives it far from him. <verse eid="PRO 22:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 22:16"/>The one oppressing the poor, to increase for himself, giving to a rich one, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 22:16">surely <char style="add">is</char> unto poverty. <verse eid="PRO 22:16"/></para>

<para style="s">Thirty Sayings of the Wise</para>

<para style="s1">Saying 1</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 22:17"/>Incline your ear and hear the words of the wise ones, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 22:17">and set your heart to my knowledge; <verse eid="PRO 22:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 22:18"/>for <char style="add">it is</char> pleasant when you guard them in your belly; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 22:18">they are established together upon your lips. <verse eid="PRO 22:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 22:19"/>For your trust to be in YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 22:19">I have caused you to know this day—even you. <verse eid="PRO 22:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 22:20"/>Have I not written to you thirty sayings<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">22.20 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">written for you excellent sayings</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">written for you three times</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 22:20">of counsels and knowledge, <verse eid="PRO 22:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 22:21"/>to make you know the truth of the words of faithfulness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 22:21">to return words of faithfulness to those sending you? <verse eid="PRO 22:21"/></para>

<para style="s1">Saying 2</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 22:22"/>You must not rob a poor one because he <char style="add">is</char> poor, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 22:22">and do not oppress an afflicted one at the gate. <verse eid="PRO 22:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 22:23"/>For YHWH will fight their fight, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 22:23">and will rob the soul of those robbing them. <verse eid="PRO 22:23"/></para>

<para style="s1">Saying 3</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 22:24"/>Do not make friends with an owner of anger, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 22:24">and with a man of rage do not go in, <verse eid="PRO 22:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 22:25"/>lest you learn his ways </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 22:25">and receive a snare for your soul. <verse eid="PRO 22:25"/></para>

<para style="s1">Saying 4</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 22:26"/>Do not be among those striking hands </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 22:26">in the pledging <char style="add">for</char> loans. <verse eid="PRO 22:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 22:27"/>If there is nothing unto you to repay, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 22:27">why should he take your bed from under you? <verse eid="PRO 22:27"/></para>

<para style="s1">Saying 5</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 22:28"/>Do not remove a boundary of old, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 22:28">which your fathers have made. <verse eid="PRO 22:28"/></para>

<para style="s1">Saying 6</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PRO 22:29"/>Do you see a man quick in his work? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 22:29">Before the face of kings he will stand; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 22:29">he will not stand before the face of obscure ones. <verse eid="PRO 22:29"/></para>

<chapter eid="PRO 22"/>

<chapter number="23" style="c" sid="PRO 23"/>

<para style="s">True Riches</para>

<para style="s1">Saying 7</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 23:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">James 5:1–6</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">1 Timothy 6:17–19</char></note>When you sit down to eat with a ruler, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 23:1">discern carefully what is before your face,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">23.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">who is before your face</char></note> <verse eid="PRO 23:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 23:2"/>and put a knife to your throat </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 23:2">if you are an owner of an appetite. <verse eid="PRO 23:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 23:3"/>You should not mark out his delicacies, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 23:3">for it is bread of lies. <verse eid="PRO 23:3"/></para>

<para style="s1">Saying 8</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 23:4"/>Do not toil to become rich, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 23:4">cease from your own understanding. <verse eid="PRO 23:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 23:5"/>Will you make your eyes fly onto it, and it is not there? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 23:5">For it certainly makes for itself wings like an eagle </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 23:5"><char style="add">and</char> flies away <char style="add">to</char> the heavens! <verse eid="PRO 23:5"/></para>

<para style="s1">Saying 9</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 23:6"/>Do not eat the bread of one evil of eye, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 23:6">and do not mark out his delicacies. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">23.6 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">of one who is stingy</char></note><verse eid="PRO 23:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 23:7"/>For like one who calculates in his soul, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 23:7">so <char style="add">is</char> he—</para>

<para style="q1" vid="PRO 23:7">“Eat and drink,” he says to you, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 23:7">and his heart <char style="add">is</char> not with you. <verse eid="PRO 23:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 23:8"/>Your morsel <char style="add">that</char> you have eaten, you will vomit it up, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 23:8">and you will ruin your pleasant words! <verse eid="PRO 23:8"/></para>

<para style="s1">Saying 10</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 23:9"/>Do not speak in the ears of a fool, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 23:9">for he will despise the wisdom of your words. <verse eid="PRO 23:9"/></para>

<para style="s1">Saying 11</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 23:10"/>Do not remove a boundary of old, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 23:10">and do not enter into the fields of the fatherless. <verse eid="PRO 23:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 23:11"/>For their Redeemer <char style="add">is</char> strong—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 23:11">He will contend their dispute against you. <verse eid="PRO 23:11"/></para>

<para style="s1">Saying 12</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 23:12"/>You must bring your heart to discipline, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 23:12">and your ears to the words of knowledge. <verse eid="PRO 23:12"/></para>

<para style="s1">Saying 13</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 23:13"/>Do not withhold discipline from a child; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 23:13">if you strike him with the rod, he will not die. <verse eid="PRO 23:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 23:14"/>You strike him with the rod, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 23:14">and you will deliver his soul from Sheol. <verse eid="PRO 23:14"/></para>

<para style="s1">Saying 14</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 23:15"/>My son, if your heart is wise, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 23:15">my heart will be glad—even I. <verse eid="PRO 23:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 23:16"/>And my kidneys will exult </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 23:16">at the speaking of uprightness <char style="add">by</char> your lips. <verse eid="PRO 23:16"/></para>

<para style="s1">Saying 15</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 23:17"/>Do not let your heart be jealous of the sinners, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 23:17">but rather in the fear of YHWH all the day. <verse eid="PRO 23:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 23:18"/>For surely there is a posterity, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 23:18">and your hope will not be cut off. <verse eid="PRO 23:18"/></para>

<para style="s1">Saying 16</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 23:19"/>Listen you, my son, and be wise, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 23:19">and let your heart walk straight in the way. <verse eid="PRO 23:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 23:20"/>Not Be among those getting drunk <char style="add">on</char> wine, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 23:20">among those being gluttons of flesh to themelves. <verse eid="PRO 23:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 23:21"/>For the drunkard and the glutton will be dispossessed, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 23:21">and drowsiness will clothe <char style="add">them</char> in rags. <verse eid="PRO 23:21"/></para>

<para style="s1">Saying 17</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 23:22"/>Listen to your father, this one begot you, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 23:22">and do not despise your mother when she is old. <verse eid="PRO 23:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 23:23"/>Acquire truth and do not sell <char style="add">it</char>—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 23:23">wisdom, and discipline, and discernment. <verse eid="PRO 23:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 23:24"/>The father of a righteous one will greatly rejoice, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 23:24">and the one begetting a wise <char style="add">son</char> will be glad in him. <verse eid="PRO 23:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 23:25"/>Let your father and your mother be glad, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 23:25">and let she who bore you rejoice. <verse eid="PRO 23:25"/></para>

<para style="s1">Saying 18</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 23:26"/>My son, give your heart to me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 23:26">and let your eyes delight <char style="add">in</char> my ways. <verse eid="PRO 23:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 23:27"/>For a prostitute <char style="add">is</char> a deep pit, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 23:27">and a strange woman <char style="add">is</char> a narrow well. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">23.27 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">a foreign woman</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">an adultress</char></note><verse eid="PRO 23:27"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 23:28"/>She also, like a robber, lies in wait, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 23:28">and she increases the treacherous ones among men. <verse eid="PRO 23:28"/></para>

<para style="s1">Saying 19</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PRO 23:29"/>To whom <char style="add">is</char> woe? To whom <char style="add">is</char> sorrow? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 23:29">To whom <char style="add">are</char> quarrels? To whom <char style="add">is</char> complaining? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 23:29">To whom <char style="add">are</char> wounds without cause? To whom <char style="add">is</char> dullness of eyes? <verse eid="PRO 23:29"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PRO 23:30"/>To those lingering over the wine, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 23:30">to those going in search of mixed drink! <verse eid="PRO 23:30"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PRO 23:31"/>Do not look <char style="add">at</char> the wine when it is red, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 23:31">when it gives forth its eye in the cup—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 23:31">it goes down with smoothness! <verse eid="PRO 23:31"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PRO 23:32"/>Its end <char style="add">is</char> like a serpent—it bites, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 23:32">and like a viper it stings. <verse eid="PRO 23:32"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="PRO 23:33"/>Your eyes will see strange things, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 23:33">and your heart will speak perverse things. <verse eid="PRO 23:33"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="PRO 23:34"/>And you will become like one lying down in the heart of the sea, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 23:34">and like one lying down on the top of a mast: <verse eid="PRO 23:34"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="PRO 23:35"/>“They struck me; I did not become weak. </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 23:35">They beat me; I did not know <char style="add">it</char>. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PRO 23:35">When I awake, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 23:35">I will add to seek it again?” <verse eid="PRO 23:35"/></para>

<chapter eid="PRO 23"/>

<chapter number="24" style="c" sid="PRO 24"/>

<para style="s">Do Not Envy</para>

<para style="s1">Saying 20</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 24:1"/>Do not be envious of men of evil, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 24:1">and do not desire to be with them, <verse eid="PRO 24:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 24:2"/>for their heart devises violence </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 24:2">and their lips speak trouble. <verse eid="PRO 24:2"/></para>

<para style="s1">Saying 21</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 24:3"/>By wisdom a house is built, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 24:3">and by understanding it is established, <verse eid="PRO 24:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 24:4"/>and by knowledge the rooms are filled </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 24:4">with all precious pleasant wealth. <verse eid="PRO 24:4"/></para>

<para style="s1">Saying 22</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 24:5"/>A man of wisdom <char style="add">is</char> strong;<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">24.5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> LXX </char><char style="fq" closed="false">The wise are mightier than the strong</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 24:5">and a man of knowledge strengthens power; <verse eid="PRO 24:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 24:6"/>for by wise counsel you can fashion for yourself the battle, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 24:6">and victory <char style="add">is</char> in a multitude counselors. <verse eid="PRO 24:6"/></para>

<para style="s1">Saying 23</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 24:7"/>Wisdom <char style="add">is</char> high for a fool; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 24:7">in the gate he does not open his mouth. <verse eid="PRO 24:7"/></para>

<para style="s1">Saying 24</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 24:8"/>One planning to do evil, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 24:8">they will call him an owner of schemes. <verse eid="PRO 24:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 24:9"/>The plotting of foolishness <char style="add">is</char> sin, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 24:9">and an abomination to man <char style="add">is</char> onemocking. <verse eid="PRO 24:9"/></para>

<para style="s1">Saying 25</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 24:10"/><char style="add">If</char> you slacken in the day of distress, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 24:10"><char style="add">then</char> narrow <char style="add">is</char> your strength. <verse eid="PRO 24:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 24:11"/>Deliver those being led away to death, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 24:11">and those stumbling to the slaughter, if only you would hold back. <verse eid="PRO 24:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 24:12"/>If you say, “Behold we did not know this,” </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 24:12">does not the One weighing hearts Himself know <char style="add">it</char>, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PRO 24:12">and the One watching over your soul Himself know it? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 24:12">And He has rendered to each man according to his work. <verse eid="PRO 24:12"/></para>

<para style="s1">Saying 26</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 24:13"/>Eat honey, my son, for <char style="add">it is</char> good, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 24:13">and the honeycomb <char style="add">is</char> sweet upon your palate. <verse eid="PRO 24:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 24:14"/>Know that wisdom <char style="add">is</char> thus to your soul; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 24:14">if you have found <char style="add">it</char>, then there is a posterity, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 24:14">and your hope will not be cut off. <verse eid="PRO 24:14"/></para>

<para style="s1">Saying 27</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 24:15"/>Do not lie in wait like a wicked one against the abode of the righteous; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 24:15">do not spoil his resting place; <verse eid="PRO 24:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 24:16"/>for seven times the righteous may fall and rise up, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 24:16">and the wicked shall stumble into evil. <verse eid="PRO 24:16"/></para>

<para style="s1">Saying 28</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 24:17"/>At the falling of your enemy, you should not be glad, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 24:17">and in his stumbling do not let your heart rejoice, <verse eid="PRO 24:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 24:18"/>lest YHWH should see and <char style="add">it be</char> evil in His eyes, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 24:18">and He turns away His anger from him. <verse eid="PRO 24:18"/></para>

<para style="s1">Saying 29</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 24:19"/>You must not fret at the evildoers, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 24:19">and do not be envious of the wicked, <verse eid="PRO 24:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 24:20"/>for there is no posterity for an evil one, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 24:20"><char style="add">and</char> the lamp of the wicked ones will be extinguished. <verse eid="PRO 24:20"/></para>

<para style="s1">Saying 30</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 24:21"/>Fear YHWH, my son, and the king; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 24:21">do not pledge yourself with ones who change, <verse eid="PRO 24:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 24:22"/>for suddenly their downfall will arise, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 24:22">and the ruin of them both—who knows? <verse eid="PRO 24:22"/></para>

<para style="s">Further Sayings of the Wise</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 24:23"/>These also are of the wise ones: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PRO 24:23">The recognizing of faces in <char style="add">giving</char> judgment </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 24:23"><char style="add">is</char> not good. <verse eid="PRO 24:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 24:24"/>One saying to a wicked one, “You <char style="add">are</char> righteous”—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 24:24">peoples will curse him; nations will denounce him; <verse eid="PRO 24:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 24:25"/>and to those reproving it will be pleasant, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 24:25">and upon them will come a blessing of goodness. <verse eid="PRO 24:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 24:26"/>The lips </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 24:26">he kisses—the one returning straightforward words. <verse eid="PRO 24:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 24:27"/>Prepare your work in the outdoors, and make it ready in the field for yourself; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 24:27">and afterward you may build your house. <verse eid="PRO 24:27"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 24:28"/>You must not be a witness without cause against your neighbor </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 24:28">or deceive with your lips. <verse eid="PRO 24:28"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PRO 24:29"/>Do not say, “According to what he has done to me, so I will do to him; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 24:29">I will return to the man according to his deed.” <verse eid="PRO 24:29"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PRO 24:30"/>Near the field of a lazy man I passed by, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 24:30">and near the vineyard of a man lacking heart. <verse eid="PRO 24:30"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PRO 24:31"/>And behold, thorns had come up all over it; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 24:31">its face was covered with nettles, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 24:31">and the wall of its stones was torn down. <verse eid="PRO 24:31"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PRO 24:32"/>And I saw—I—I set my heart; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 24:32">I have seen, I have received instruction. <verse eid="PRO 24:32"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="PRO 24:33"/>A little sleep, a little slumber, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 24:33">a little a folding of the hands to rest, <verse eid="PRO 24:33"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="PRO 24:34"/>and your poverty has come <char style="add">as</char> one traveling, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 24:34">and your needs like a man of shield. <verse eid="PRO 24:34"/></para>

<chapter eid="PRO 24"/>

<chapter number="25" style="c" sid="PRO 25"/>

<para style="s">More Proverbs of Solomon</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 25:1"/>These also <char style="add">are</char> proverbs of Solomon, which the men of Hezekiah king of Judah copied down: <verse eid="PRO 25:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 25:2"/>The glory of God <char style="add">is</char> to conceal a matter, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 25:2">and the glory of kings <char style="add">is</char> to search out a matter. <verse eid="PRO 25:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 25:3"/>The heavens for height and the earth for depth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 25:3">and the heart of kings cannot be searched. <verse eid="PRO 25:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 25:4"/>Remove the dross from the silver, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 25:4">and a vessel will come forth for the refiner. <verse eid="PRO 25:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 25:5"/>Remove the wicked before the face of the king, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 25:5">and his throne will be established in righteousness. <verse eid="PRO 25:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 25:6"/>You should not exalt yourself before the face of the king, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 25:6">and in the place of the great ones you should not stand. <verse eid="PRO 25:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 25:7"/>For better that he says to you “Come up here!” </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 25:7">Than to set you low before a noble. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PRO 25:7">That which your eyes have seen, <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">25.7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Whom</char></note><verse eid="PRO 25:7"/></para>

<para style="q2"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 25:8"/>you should not go out to dispute hastily, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PRO 25:8">for what will you do in the end </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 25:8">when your neighbor has put you to shame? <verse eid="PRO 25:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 25:9"/>Dispute your cause with your neighbor, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 25:9">and do not uncover the secret to another, <verse eid="PRO 25:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 25:10"/>lest the one hearing <char style="add">it</char> should bring shame to you, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 25:10">and your defamation shall not turn back. <verse eid="PRO 25:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 25:11"/>Apples of gold in figures of silver, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 25:11"><char style="add">is</char> a word spoken at its right time. <verse eid="PRO 25:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 25:12"/>A ring of gold and an ornament of fine gold, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 25:12"><char style="add">is</char> a wise one giving rebuke to a listening ear. <verse eid="PRO 25:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 25:13"/>Like the cold of snow in time of harvest, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 25:13"><char style="add">is</char> a faithful messenger to those sending him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 25:13">and he restores the soul of his lords. <verse eid="PRO 25:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 25:14"/>Clouds and wind and no rain, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 25:14"><char style="add">is</char> a man boasting in gifts of deception. <verse eid="PRO 25:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 25:15"/>With slowness of anger a ruler may be persuaded, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 25:15">and a gentle tongue can break a bone. <verse eid="PRO 25:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 25:16"/>You have found honey, eat your sufficiency, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 25:16">lest you be filled up with it and vomit it out. <verse eid="PRO 25:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 25:17"/>Make rare your foot from the house of your neighbor, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 25:17">lest he have his fill of you and hate you. <verse eid="PRO 25:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 25:18"/>A club or a sharpened sword, or an arrow, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 25:18"><char style="add">is</char> a man answering against his neighbor a testimony of falsehood. <verse eid="PRO 25:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 25:19"/>A tooth broken or a foot tottering </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 25:19"><char style="add">is</char> trust in one acting treacherously in a day of distress. <verse eid="PRO 25:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 25:20"/>One taking away a garment in a day of cold, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 25:20"><char style="add">or</char> vinegar on soda,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">25.20 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">on a wound</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 25:20"><char style="add">is</char> one singing with songs to a heart of misery. <verse eid="PRO 25:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 25:21"/>If your enemy <char style="add">is</char> hungry, give him bread, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 25:21">and if <char style="add">he is</char> thirsty, give him water to drink, <verse eid="PRO 25:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 25:22"/>For <char style="add">in so doing</char> you will be heaping burning coals upon his head, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 25:22">and YHWH will give recompense to you. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">25.22 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> LXX; Hebrew </char><char style="fq" closed="false">for you will heap burning coals on his head</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; cited in Romans 12:20</char></note><verse eid="PRO 25:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 25:23"/>A north wind twists out rain, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 25:23">and a secret tongue <char style="add">brings</char> faces of indignanation. <verse eid="PRO 25:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 25:24"/>Better to sit on the corner of roof, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 25:24">than with a wife of quarrels and a house of company. <verse eid="PRO 25:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 25:25"/>Cold water over a weary soul, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 25:25"><char style="add">is</char> good news from a land far away. <verse eid="PRO 25:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 25:26"/>A spring made foul or a well spoiled </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 25:26"><char style="add">is</char> a righteous one swaying before the face of a wicked one. <verse eid="PRO 25:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 25:27"/>To eat much honey <char style="add">is</char> not good, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 25:27"><char style="add">nor</char> the searching for his own honor. <verse eid="PRO 25:27"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 25:28"/>A city breached, without a wall, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 25:28"><char style="add">is</char> a man who <char style="add">is</char> without restraint to his spirit. <verse eid="PRO 25:28"/></para>

<chapter eid="PRO 25"/>

<chapter number="26" style="c" sid="PRO 26"/>

<para style="s">Similitudes and Instructions</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 26:1"/>Like the snow in the summer, and like the rain in the harvest, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 26:1">so honor is not fitting for a fool. <verse eid="PRO 26:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 26:2"/>Like the sparrow in fluttering, like the swallow in flying, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 26:2">so a curse without cause does not come. <verse eid="PRO 26:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 26:3"/>A whip for the horse, a bridle for the donkey, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 26:3">and a rod for the back of fools! <verse eid="PRO 26:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 26:4"/>Do not answer a fool according to his folly, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 26:4">lest you be likened to him—even you. <verse eid="PRO 26:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 26:5"/>Answer a fool according to his folly, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 26:5">lest he become wise in his eyes. <verse eid="PRO 26:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 26:6"/>Cutting off feet, drinking violence, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 26:6"><char style="add">is</char> sending a message by the hand of fool. <verse eid="PRO 26:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 26:7"/>Legs hanging limp from lameness </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 26:7"><char style="add">is</char> a proverb in the mouth of fools. <verse eid="PRO 26:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 26:8"/>Binding up a stone in a sling, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 26:8">so <char style="add">is</char> giving honor to a fool. <verse eid="PRO 26:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 26:9"/>A thorn <char style="add">that</char> goes into the hand of a drunkard, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 26:9">so <char style="add">is</char> a proverb in the mouth of fools. <verse eid="PRO 26:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 26:10"/>An archer piercing anything, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 26:10">so <char style="add">is</char> hiring a fool or hiring those passing by. <verse eid="PRO 26:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 26:11"/>Like a dog returning to its vomit </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 26:11"><char style="add">is</char> a fool repeating his folly. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">26.11 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Cited in 2 Peter 2:22</char></note><verse eid="PRO 26:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 26:12"/>Do you see a man wise in his eyes? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 26:12">Hope <char style="add">is</char> for a fool more than him. <verse eid="PRO 26:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 26:13"/>A lazy one says, “A lion <char style="add">is</char> in the road! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 26:13">A fierce lion <char style="add">is</char> in the broad places!” <verse eid="PRO 26:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 26:14"/>The door <char style="add">that</char> turns about on its hinges, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 26:14">so <char style="add">is</char> a lazy one upon his bed. <verse eid="PRO 26:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 26:15"/>A lazy one hides his hand in the bowl; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 26:15">it wearies him to bring it back to his mouth. <verse eid="PRO 26:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 26:16"/>Wiser <char style="add">is</char> a lazy one in his eyes, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 26:16">than seven returning a reason. <verse eid="PRO 26:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 26:17"/>One grabbing hold on the ears of a dog passing by, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 26:17"><char style="add">is</char> a passerby in a quarrel not unto him. <verse eid="PRO 26:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 26:18"/>Like a madman shooting firebrands </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 26:18">arrows, and death, <verse eid="PRO 26:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 26:19"/>so <char style="add">is</char> the man who has deceived his neighbor, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 26:19">and he says, “Am I not playing?” <verse eid="PRO 26:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 26:20"/>With the end of the wood, the fire <char style="add">is</char> quenched, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 26:20">and without one whispering, strife quiets down. <verse eid="PRO 26:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 26:21"/>Charcoal to burning coals, and wood to a fire, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 26:21">so <char style="add">is</char> a man of quarrels to kindle strife. <verse eid="PRO 26:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 26:22"/>The words of one whispering <char style="add">are</char> like morsels being swallowed, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 26:22">they even go down <char style="add">to</char> the chambers of the belly. <verse eid="PRO 26:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 26:23"/>Silver of dross laid over an earthen vessel </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 26:23"><char style="add">are</char> burning<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">26.23 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Hebrew; LXX </char><char style="fq" closed="false">smooth</char></note> lips and a heart of evil. <verse eid="PRO 26:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 26:24"/>With his lips the one hating disguises <char style="add">it</char>, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 26:24">and within himself he places deceit. <verse eid="PRO 26:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 26:25"/>When his voice is favorable, you should not trust in him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 26:25">for seven abominations <char style="add">are</char> in his heart. <verse eid="PRO 26:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 26:26"/>Hatred is concealed by deceit; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 26:26">his wickedness will be uncovered in the assembly. <verse eid="PRO 26:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 26:27"/>The one digging a pit, he will fall into it; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 26:27">and the one rolling a stone, to him it will return. <verse eid="PRO 26:27"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 26:28"/>A tongue of deceit hates its oppressed ones, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 26:28">and a smooth mouth causes ruin. <verse eid="PRO 26:28"/></para>

<chapter eid="PRO 26"/>

<chapter number="27" style="c" sid="PRO 27"/>

<para style="s">Do Not Boast about Tomorrow</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 27:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">James 4:13–17</char></note>Do not boast about tomorrow </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 27:1">for, you do not know what a day will bring forth. <verse eid="PRO 27:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 27:2"/>Let a stranger praise you, and not your own mouth—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 27:2">a foreigner, and not your own lips. <verse eid="PRO 27:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 27:3"/>The heaviness of a stone and the weight of the sand—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 27:3">and the anger of a fool <char style="add">is</char> heavier than both of them. <verse eid="PRO 27:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 27:4"/>The cruelty of rage and the flood of a nostril—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 27:4">and who can stand before the face of jealousy? <verse eid="PRO 27:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 27:5"/>Better <char style="add">is</char> an uncovered rebuke </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 27:5">than love hidden. <verse eid="PRO 27:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 27:6"/>Faithful <char style="add">are</char> the wounds of one who loves, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 27:6">and abundant are the kisses of one hating. <verse eid="PRO 27:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 27:7"/>A soul satiated would trample a honeycomb, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 27:7">and <char style="add">to</char> a hungry soul, everything bitter <char style="add">is</char> sweet. <verse eid="PRO 27:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 27:8"/>Like a bird wandering from her nest, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 27:8">so <char style="add">is</char> a man wandering from his place. <verse eid="PRO 27:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 27:9"/>Oil and incense gladden the heart, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 27:9">and the sweetness of one’s friend is from the counsel of the soul. <verse eid="PRO 27:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 27:10"/>Do not forsake your friend, and the friend of your father, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 27:10">and do not enter the house of your brother </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 27:10">in the day of your calamity; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PRO 27:10">better a neighbor nearby </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 27:10">than a brother far away. <verse eid="PRO 27:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 27:11"/>Be wise, my son, and gladden my heart, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 27:11">that I may return a word to the one reproaching me. <verse eid="PRO 27:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 27:12"/>A prudent one sees evil <char style="add">coming</char>; he hides himself; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 27:12">simple ones pass along, <char style="add">and</char> they are punished. <verse eid="PRO 27:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 27:13"/>Take his garment when a stranger posts security, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 27:13">and hold it in pledge for a foreign woman.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">27.13 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">a wayward woman</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">an adultress</char></note> <verse eid="PRO 27:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 27:14"/>The one blessing his friend with a loud voice, rising early in the morning, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 27:14">it will be counted <char style="add">as</char> a curse for him. <verse eid="PRO 27:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 27:15"/>A continual dripping in a day of rain, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 27:15">and a woman of quarrels are alike— <verse eid="PRO 27:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 27:16"/>hiding her is hiding the wind </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 27:16">or grasping oil with one’s right hand. <verse eid="PRO 27:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 27:17"/>Iron is sharpened by iron, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 27:17">and a man sharpens the face of his friend. <verse eid="PRO 27:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 27:18"/>One keeping watch over a fig tree will eat its fruit, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 27:18">and the one guarding his master will be honored. <verse eid="PRO 27:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 27:19"/>As <char style="add">in</char> the water the face <char style="add">is</char> to the face, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 27:19">so the heart of the man <char style="add">is</char> to the man. <verse eid="PRO 27:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 27:20"/>Sheol and Abaddon<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">27.20 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Death and Destruction</char></note> are never satisfied, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 27:20">and the eyes of the man are never satisfied. <verse eid="PRO 27:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 27:21"/>A crucible for silver and a furnace for gold, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 27:21">so is a man by the mouth of one who praises him. <verse eid="PRO 27:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 27:22"/>Though you may pound a fool in the mortar, in the midst of the grain with the pestle, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 27:22">his folly will not turn away from him. <verse eid="PRO 27:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 27:23"/>Be sure to know the faces of your flock, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 27:23"><char style="add">and</char> set your heart to your herds, <verse eid="PRO 27:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 27:24"/>for riches <char style="add">are</char> not forever, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 27:24">nor <char style="add">is</char> a diadem for all generations. <verse eid="PRO 27:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 27:25"/>The hay is uncovered, and the tender grass is visible, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 27:25">and the herbs of the mountains are gathered. <verse eid="PRO 27:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 27:26"/>The lambs <char style="add">are</char> for your clothing, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 27:26">and the goats the price of field, <verse eid="PRO 27:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 27:27"/>and enough milk of goats <char style="add">is</char> for your foor, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 27:27">for the food of your house and the life of your maidservants. <verse eid="PRO 27:27"/></para>

<chapter eid="PRO 27"/>

<chapter number="28" style="c" sid="PRO 28"/>

<para style="s">The Boldness of the Righteous</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 28:1"/>The wicked flee and no one is pursuing, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 28:1">and the righteous are confident as a young lion. <verse eid="PRO 28:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 28:2"/>In the transgression of the land, many <char style="add">are</char> its princes; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 28:2">and with one man understanding <char style="add">and</char> knowing, so it will last long. <verse eid="PRO 28:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 28:3"/>A man being poor and oppressing the lowly ones </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 28:3"><char style="add">is like</char> a rain beating down and <char style="add">there is</char> no bread. <verse eid="PRO 28:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 28:4"/>Those abandoning instruction praise a wicked one, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 28:4">and those guarding instruction contend with them. <verse eid="PRO 28:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 28:5"/>Men of evil do not understand justice, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 28:5">and those seeking YHWH understand all. <verse eid="PRO 28:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 28:6"/>Better one being poor walking in his integrity, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 28:6">than one crooked in <char style="add">his</char> ways, and he <char style="add">is</char> rich. <verse eid="PRO 28:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 28:7"/>One watching over the law <char style="add">is</char> a discerning son, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 28:7">and one associating with gluttons disgraces his father. <verse eid="PRO 28:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 28:8"/>The one multiplying his wealth by interest and usury </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 28:8">gathers it for one showing favor to lowly ones. <verse eid="PRO 28:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 28:9"/>One turning aside his ear from hearing instruction, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 28:9">even his prayer is an abomination. <verse eid="PRO 28:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 28:10"/>One causing the upright to stray onto a path of evil, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 28:10">into his pit he himself will fall, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 28:10">and the blameless ones will inherit good <char style="add">things</char>. <verse eid="PRO 28:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 28:11"/>A rich man <char style="add">is</char> wise in his own eyes, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 28:11">and a poor one being discerning will search him out. <verse eid="PRO 28:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 28:12"/>In the rejoicing of the righteous <char style="add">is</char> great beauty, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 28:12">and in the rising up of wicked ones, a man hides himself. <verse eid="PRO 28:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 28:13"/>One covering his transgressions will not prosper, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 28:13">and one confessing and forsaking <char style="add">them</char> will find mercy. <verse eid="PRO 28:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 28:14"/>Blessed <char style="add">is</char> the man being reverent continually, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 28:14">and the one hardening his heart will fall into distress. <verse eid="PRO 28:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 28:15"/>A roaring lion and a rushing bear, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 28:15"><char style="add">is</char> a wicked ruler over a poor people. <verse eid="PRO 28:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 28:16"/>A leader lacking <char style="add">in</char> understanding <char style="add">is</char> also abundant of oppressions; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 28:16">one hating dishonest gain prolongs days. <verse eid="PRO 28:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 28:17"/>A man pressed down by the bloodshed of a soul </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 28:17">will flee into the Pit,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">28.17 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">will be a fugitive until death</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 28:17"><char style="add">with</char> none grabbing hold of him. <verse eid="PRO 28:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 28:18"/>One walking blamelessly will be saved, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 28:18">and one crooked in <char style="add">his</char> ways will fall at once. <verse eid="PRO 28:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 28:19"/>The one working his land will be filled <char style="add">with</char> bread, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 28:19">and the one pursuing empty <char style="add">things</char> will be filled with poverty. <verse eid="PRO 28:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 28:20"/>A man of faithfulness <char style="add">has</char> an abundance of blessings, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 28:20">and the one hurrying to be rich will not be acquitted. <verse eid="PRO 28:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 28:21"/>To regard faces <char style="add">is</char> not good, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 28:21">and over a morsel of bread a strong man will transgress. <verse eid="PRO 28:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 28:22"/>A man of an evil eye is panicked for wealth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 28:22">and he does not know that poverty will come upon him. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">28.22 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">A stingy man</char></note><verse eid="PRO 28:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 28:23"/>The one rebuking a man, afterward he will find favor </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 28:23">more than one being smooth of tongue. <verse eid="PRO 28:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 28:24"/>One robbing his father or his mother and saying, “There is no transgression,” </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 28:24">he <char style="add">is</char> a companion to the man bringing ruin. <verse eid="PRO 28:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 28:25"/>Being wide of appetite stirs up strife, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 28:25">and one trusting upon YHWH will be made fat. <verse eid="PRO 28:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 28:26"/>The one trusting in his heart, he <char style="add">is</char> a fool, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 28:26">and the one walking in wisdom, he will be delivered. <verse eid="PRO 28:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 28:27"/>One giving to the poor will not lack, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 28:27">and one hiding his eyes <char style="add">has</char> an abundance of curses. <verse eid="PRO 28:27"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 28:28"/>With the rising up of the wicked, a man hides himself, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 28:28">and with their perishing the righteous multiply. <verse eid="PRO 28:28"/></para>

<chapter eid="PRO 28"/>

<chapter number="29" style="c" sid="PRO 29"/>

<para style="s">The Flourishing of the Righteous</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 29:1"/>A man often reproved hardening the neck, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 29:1">suddenly will be broken, and there is no healing. <verse eid="PRO 29:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 29:2"/>With the increasing of the righteous ones, the people rejoice; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 29:2">and with the ruling of a wicked one, the people groan. <verse eid="PRO 29:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 29:3"/>A man loving wisdom gladdens his father, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 29:3">and a companion of prostitutes destroys wealth. <verse eid="PRO 29:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 29:4"/>A king by justice establishes the land, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 29:4">and a man of contributions<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">29.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">a man who taxes heavily</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">a man who takes bribes</char></note> tears it down. <verse eid="PRO 29:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 29:5"/>A man taking a portion over his neighbor </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 29:5">spreads out a net over his steps. <verse eid="PRO 29:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 29:6"/>By transgression, a man of evil is snared, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 29:6">and a righteous one sings out and rejoices. <verse eid="PRO 29:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 29:7"/>A righteous one knows the cause of the poor; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 29:7">a wicked one does not does understand knowledge. <verse eid="PRO 29:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 29:8"/>Men of scorning inflame a city, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 29:8">and wise men turn back anger. <verse eid="PRO 29:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 29:9"/>A wise man enters into judgment with a foolish man, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 29:9">and he trembles and laughs, and <char style="add">there is</char> no rest. <verse eid="PRO 29:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 29:10"/>Men of blood hate a blameless one, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 29:10">and upright ones seek his soul.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">29.10 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">upright ones care for his life</char></note> <verse eid="PRO 29:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 29:11"/>A fool brings out all his spirit, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 29:11">and a wise one soothes it backward. <verse eid="PRO 29:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 29:12"/>One ruling listening to words of deception, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 29:12">all his ministers <char style="add">are</char> wicked. <verse eid="PRO 29:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 29:13"/>The poor one and the man of oppression meet together: </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 29:13">YHWH gives light to the eyes of both of them. <verse eid="PRO 29:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 29:14"/>A king judging the poor with truth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 29:14">his throne will be established forever. <verse eid="PRO 29:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 29:15"/>A rod and rebuke give wisdom, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 29:15">and a child let away brings shame to his mother. <verse eid="PRO 29:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 29:16"/>With the increase of the wicked, transgression increases, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 29:16">and righteous ones will look on their fall. <verse eid="PRO 29:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 29:17"/>Discipline your son, and he will give you rest, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 29:17">and he will give delights to your soul. <verse eid="PRO 29:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 29:18"/>When there is no vision, the people are let loose, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 29:18">and the one keeping the Law <char style="add">is</char> blessed. <verse eid="PRO 29:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 29:19"/>With words a servant will not be disciplined; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 29:19">for he understands, yet he will not respond. <verse eid="PRO 29:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 29:20"/>Look upon a man being hasty in his words—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 29:20">the hope of a fool <char style="add">is</char> more than his. <verse eid="PRO 29:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 29:21"/>One is pampering his servant from youth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 29:21">and his end will be insolence. <verse eid="PRO 29:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 29:22"/>A man of anger stirs up strife, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 29:22">and a man of rage, much transgression. <verse eid="PRO 29:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 29:23"/>The pride of man will bring him low, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 29:23">and the one lowly of spirit will grasp honor. <verse eid="PRO 29:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 29:24"/>One having a portion with a thief is hating his own soul; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 29:24">he hears the curse, and does not testify. <verse eid="PRO 29:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 29:25"/>The fear of man sets a snare, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 29:25">and one trusting in YHWH will be set on high. <verse eid="PRO 29:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 29:26"/>Many are seeking the favor of a ruler, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 29:26">and from YHWH <char style="add">is</char> justice for a man. <verse eid="PRO 29:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 29:27"/>A man of injustice <char style="add">is</char> an abomination to righteous ones, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 29:27">and the one upright in <char style="add">his</char> way <char style="add">is</char> an abomination to a wicked one. <verse eid="PRO 29:27"/></para>

<chapter eid="PRO 29"/>

<chapter number="30" style="c" sid="PRO 30"/>

<para style="s">The Words of Agur</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 30:1"/>The words of Agur son of Jakeh—the burden. An utterance of the strong man to Ithiel; to Ithiel and Ucal.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">30.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">declared to Ithiel: “I am weary, O God, and am consumed.</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> (revocalizations)</char></note> <verse eid="PRO 30:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 30:2"/>“Surely I <char style="add">am</char> more brutish than man, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 30:2">and the understanding of man <char style="add">is</char> not unto me. <verse eid="PRO 30:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 30:3"/>And I have not learned wisdom </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 30:3">or known the knowledge of holy ones. <verse eid="PRO 30:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 30:4"/>Who has gone up <char style="add">to</char> the heavens and descended? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 30:4">Who has gathered the wind in His fists? </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PRO 30:4">Who has bound the waters in His cloak? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 30:4">Who has established all the ends of the earth? </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PRO 30:4">What <char style="add">is</char> His name, and what <char style="add">is</char> the name of His Son? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 30:4">Surely you must know! <verse eid="PRO 30:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 30:5"/>Every word of God is refined; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 30:5">He <char style="add">is</char> a shield for those taking refuge in Him. <verse eid="PRO 30:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 30:6"/>Do not add to His words, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 30:6">lest He rebuke you, and you be found a liar. <verse eid="PRO 30:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 30:7"/>Two <char style="add">things</char> I have asked of You—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 30:7">do not withhold <char style="add">them</char> from me before I die: <verse eid="PRO 30:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 30:8"/>Put vanity and the word of a lie far away from me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 30:8">do not give poverty or wealth to me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 30:8">provide me the bread of my portion, <verse eid="PRO 30:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 30:9"/>lest I become satisfied </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 30:9">and I deny and say, ‘Who <char style="add">is</char> YHWH?’ </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PRO 30:9">And lest I become dispossessed and steal, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 30:9">and I seize the name of my God. <verse eid="PRO 30:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 30:10"/>Do not slander a servant to his master, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 30:10">lest he curse you and you be found guilty. <verse eid="PRO 30:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 30:11"/>A generation lightly esteems its father, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 30:11">and does not bless its mother. <verse eid="PRO 30:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 30:12"/>A generation <char style="add">is</char> pure in its own eyes </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 30:12">and yet has not been washed from its filth. <verse eid="PRO 30:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 30:13"/>A generation—how high its eyes, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 30:13">and its eyelids are lifted up! <verse eid="PRO 30:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 30:14"/>A generation—its teeth <char style="add">are</char> swords </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 30:14">and its fangs <char style="add">are</char> knives, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PRO 30:14">to devour the poor from the earth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 30:14">and needy ones from mankind. <verse eid="PRO 30:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 30:15"/>Unto the leech <char style="add">are</char> two daughters—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 30:15">‘Give, <char style="add">and</char> Give. </para>

<para style="p" vid="PRO 30:15">Three <char style="add">things</char> are never satisfied, four never say, ‘Enough!’: <verse eid="PRO 30:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 30:16"/>Sheol, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PRO 30:16">and the barren womb, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PRO 30:16">earth not satisfied with water, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PRO 30:16">and the fire never having said, ‘Enough!’ <verse eid="PRO 30:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 30:17"/>The eye <char style="add">that</char> mocks at a father </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 30:17">and despises obedience to a mother—</para>

<para style="q1" vid="PRO 30:17">the ravens of the valley will dig it out, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 30:17">and the young eagles will eat it. <verse eid="PRO 30:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 30:18"/>Three <char style="add">things</char>, they are wonderful for me, and four, I cannot know them: <verse eid="PRO 30:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 30:19"/>The way of an eagle in the heavens, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PRO 30:19">the way of a snake on a rock, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PRO 30:19">the way of a ship in the midst of the sea, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PRO 30:19">and the way of a man with a maiden. <verse eid="PRO 30:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 30:20"/>This <char style="add">is</char> the way of a woman committing adultery: </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 30:20">She eats and has wiped her mouth </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 30:20">and has said, ‘I have not done wickedness.’ <verse eid="PRO 30:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 30:21"/>For three things the earth has trembled, and for four it is not able to bear up: <verse eid="PRO 30:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 30:22"/>Under a servant when he becomes king, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PRO 30:22">and a fool when he is filled with food, <verse eid="PRO 30:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 30:23"/>under a hated woman when she is married, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PRO 30:23">and a maidservant when she dispossesses her mistress. <verse eid="PRO 30:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 30:24"/>Four <char style="add">things</char>, they <char style="add">are</char> small on the earth; they are wiser than wise: <verse eid="PRO 30:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 30:25"/>The ants <char style="add">are</char> a people not strong, and they prepare their food in the summer; <verse eid="PRO 30:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 30:26"/>the rock badgers<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">30.26 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the coneys</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the hyraxes</char></note> <char style="add">are</char> a people not strong, and they set their home in the cliffs; <verse eid="PRO 30:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 30:27"/>a king <char style="add">is</char> not unto the locust, and go they forth in formation, all of them; <verse eid="PRO 30:27"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 30:28"/>the lizard can be caught in one’s hands, and it <char style="add">is</char> in the palaces of king. <verse eid="PRO 30:28"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PRO 30:29"/>Three <char style="add">things</char>, they <char style="add">are</char> are doing well of step, even four are doing well in the walk: <verse eid="PRO 30:29"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PRO 30:30"/>A lion, mighty among the beasts, and it does not turn back from the face of anything; <verse eid="PRO 30:30"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PRO 30:31"/>one girded of loins, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PRO 30:31">or a he-goat, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PRO 30:31">and a king with his army around him.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">30.31 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">a king against whom there is no rising up</char></note> <verse eid="PRO 30:31"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PRO 30:32"/>If you have been foolish in lifting up yourself, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 30:32">and if you have schemed—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 30:32">hand to mouth! <verse eid="PRO 30:32"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="PRO 30:33"/>For <char style="add">as</char> the churning of milk brings forth butter, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 30:33">and pressing of the nose brings forth blood, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 30:33">so the pressing of anger brings forth strife.” <verse eid="PRO 30:33"/></para>

<chapter eid="PRO 30"/>

<chapter number="31" style="c" sid="PRO 31"/>

<para style="s">The Sayings for King Lemuel</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PRO 31:1"/>The words of Lemuel the king—the burden that his mother taught him: <verse eid="PRO 31:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PRO 31:2"/>What, O my son? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 31:2">And what, O son of my womb? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 31:2">And what, O son of my vows? <verse eid="PRO 31:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PRO 31:3"/>Do not give your strength to the women, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 31:3">and your ways to wiping away kings. <verse eid="PRO 31:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PRO 31:4"/>Not for kings, O Lemuel, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 31:4"><char style="add">it is</char> not for kings to drink wine, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 31:4">nor for rulers strong drink, <verse eid="PRO 31:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PRO 31:5"/>lest they drink and forget the decree, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 31:5">and pervert the judgment of any of the sons of affliction. <verse eid="PRO 31:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PRO 31:6"/>Give strong drink to the one perishing, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 31:6">and wine to those bitter of soul. <verse eid="PRO 31:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PRO 31:7"/>Let him drink and forget his poverty, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 31:7">and not remember his trouble anymore. <verse eid="PRO 31:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PRO 31:8"/>Open your mouth for a mute one, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 31:8">for the cause of all the sons of destitution. <verse eid="PRO 31:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PRO 31:9"/>Open your mouth, judge with righteousness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 31:9">and plead the cause of the poor one and needy one. <verse eid="PRO 31:9"/></para>

<para style="s">The Virtues of a Noble Woman</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PRO 31:10"/>A wife<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">31.10 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Verses 10–31 are an acrostic poem, each verse beginning with the successive letters of the Hebrew alphabet.</char></note> of worth, who can find <char style="add">her</char>? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 31:10">And far above rubies <char style="add">is</char> her value. <verse eid="PRO 31:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PRO 31:11"/>The heart of her husband trusts in her, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 31:11">and he is not lacking <char style="add">in</char> spoil. <verse eid="PRO 31:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PRO 31:12"/>She has done him good, and not evil, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 31:12">all the days of her life. <verse eid="PRO 31:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PRO 31:13"/>She has sought wool and flax, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 31:13">and she works <char style="add">it</char> with the delight of her palms. <verse eid="PRO 31:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PRO 31:14"/>She is like the ships of a merchant—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 31:14">from afar she brings <char style="add">in</char> her bread. <verse eid="PRO 31:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PRO 31:15"/>And she rises and it is still night, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 31:15">and she provides food for her house, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 31:15">even the portion assigned to her maidservants. <verse eid="PRO 31:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PRO 31:16"/>She considers a field and buys it; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 31:16">from the fruit of her palms she plants a vineyard. <verse eid="PRO 31:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PRO 31:17"/>She girds her loins with strength </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 31:17">and strengthens her arms. <verse eid="PRO 31:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PRO 31:18"/>She tastes that her profit <char style="add">is</char> good; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 31:18">her lamp is not extinguished in the night. <verse eid="PRO 31:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PRO 31:19"/>She stretched out her hands to the distaff, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 31:19">and her palms grasp the spindle. <verse eid="PRO 31:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PRO 31:20"/>Her palm she spreads out to a poor one, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 31:20">and her hands she sends out to a needy one. <verse eid="PRO 31:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PRO 31:21"/>She does not fear for her house because of snow, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 31:21">for all her house <char style="add">is</char> clothed in scarlet.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">31.21 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">is doubly clothed</char></note> <verse eid="PRO 31:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PRO 31:22"/>Coverings she has made for herself; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 31:22">fine linen and purple <char style="add">are</char> her clothing. <verse eid="PRO 31:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PRO 31:23"/>Her husband is known in the gates, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 31:23">in his sitting with the elders of the land. <verse eid="PRO 31:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PRO 31:24"/>Linen garments she has made and sold, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 31:24">and a girdle she gives to the merchant. <verse eid="PRO 31:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PRO 31:25"/>Strength and honor <char style="add">are</char> her clothing, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 31:25">and she laughs at the day to come. <verse eid="PRO 31:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PRO 31:26"/>She opens her mouth with wisdom, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 31:26">and instruction of kindness <char style="add">is</char> on her tongue. <verse eid="PRO 31:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PRO 31:27"/>She watches the goings of her house, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 31:27">and the bread of idleness she does not eat. <verse eid="PRO 31:27"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PRO 31:28"/>Her children rise up and call her blessed, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 31:28">and her husband he praises her: <verse eid="PRO 31:28"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PRO 31:29"/>“Many daughters have acted with worth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 31:29">and you have gone up over them all.” <verse eid="PRO 31:29"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PRO 31:30"/>Charm <char style="add">is</char> deceptive and beauty <char style="add">is</char> vapor, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 31:30">and a woman fearing YHWH—she is to be praised. <verse eid="PRO 31:30"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PRO 31:31"/>Give to her from the fruit of her hands, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PRO 31:31">and let her own deeds praise her in the gates. <verse eid="PRO 31:31"/></para>

<chapter eid="PRO 31"/>

</usx>
